s://api.github.com/users/ushkarev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ministryofjustice/hmpps-micro-frontend-components/commits/892a9cb44f912da176cb5fb82c20a213753da40c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T14:50:51Z","email":"ushkarev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ushkarev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T14:50:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix width variable for govuk-frontend 6.2 (#611)\n\nNotably, the footer component’s width was set incorrectly whereas the header was fine. This is related to the differing scss imports and their order.\n\nBefore: both components included a style for `.govuk-width-container` (but footer did not pick up width override variable)\nNow: neither component includes `.govuk-width-container`\n\nThis is a breaking change, but including govuk-frontend styles should sensibly be left to clients to concern themselves with? DPS applications already should set the width variables themselves.\n\nThe theory is that the footer’s `@import ''govuk-frontend/dist/govuk/objects/width-container''` used to transitively import `govuk-frontend/dist/govuk/base` but has stopped doing so in 6.2","tree":{"sha":"f1a6e6b00ed7f0b684b5b5501a5443d299aed107","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ministryofjustice/hmpps-micro-frontend-components/git/trees/f1a6e6b00ed7f0b684b5b5501a5443d299aed107"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ministryofjustice/hmpps-micro-frontend-components/git/commits/892a9cb44f912da176cb5fb82c20a213753da40c","verification":{"payload":"tree f1a6e6b00ed7f0b684b5b5501a5443d299aed107\nparent 7d620ff3ac125f79b5d06ae8ac3e3cfc77622313\nauthor ushkarev <ushkarev@users.noreply.github.com> 1781103051 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781103051 +0100\n\nFix width variable for govuk-frontend 6.2 (#611)\n\nNotably, the footer component’s width was set incorrectly whereas the header was fine. This is related to the differing scss imports and their order.\n\nBefore: both components included a style for `.govuk-width-container` (but footer did not pick up width override variable)\nNow: neither component includes `.govuk-width-container`\n\nThis is a breaking change, but including govuk-frontend styles should sensibly be left to clients to concern themselves with? DPS applications already should set the width variables themselves.\n\nThe theory is that the footer’s `@import ''govuk-frontend/dist/govuk/objects/width-container''` used to transitively import `govuk-frontend/dist/govuk/base` but has stopped doing so in 6.2","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKXnLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANKgQAKqDkyyEbHyMDw0jdsHULYsi\nmxvp7acY7zWW6KuKMtfLJoPXuZe4z3KT95352zDYi1BbHUJ1vjcWYfFGlFW4bWwS\n+slzHV7TlfibSH2wu3/hdvUZP/v5bttuuK92iEvcvOz2uKBt6IfIOmyvrCM2/Abx\nU2k/6DKuyV/bSYQObVRoP788FOTzedak9u352eh6NAuiVcvBluFH4i8EKxz10SKV\nj6knUtgSeSKfTCAaevbVCPoITsJMnjdAdFToYEg/aNwyUWOrWBFN+Xq2RI0vVmRu\nf9c0fm6FW2yXTqQWSmqN2zGoVoBIylKkvseNNLdgae/lVAWW0RKyUmCF3XgKGnd0\nBM+TaYYsp+YR7urQgP72QkFKLc9Do+sRKGBmosZu/8rp4yA/TeWNvDl28kNGHQ5y\nB9CTnbQOENDCbfzckHsLavOTPC+XYNdQRDdyaR4cciT4JnsEN5o5Nu7bhhfj7A9H\nI82pvn66uTePXFoxbAtvPvOyavOV6Qk+9hYGO/BmTod2AXu+Q+PfSyJuiE98JlQe\nS4GwDqWCejvRoRm8L5pOnoBMTOA73uWBwPD8Oq7fxc0Qlrr7MJg6/HpxoQ81PFN4\nNkXWuRx44OxMmGMjn5HQTpWbm3qxySoovyIm7fTKYC0bpeHZFr/78eLhCdrcWiYT\nXemeOwiEeERiUDKe6JBL\n=H87k\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-10T14:50:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"h