endabot updates\n\nFolds all 12 open Dependabot PRs into one change: eslint 8 -> 10 with the .eslintrc ->\nflat config migration, typescript-eslint 7 -> 8 (8.67 rather than 8.48, whose peer range\nexcludes eslint 10), react-router 7.18 and form-data 4.0.6. Five of the PRs were stale.\n\nCloses #859\n\n* chore(deps): restore form-data 4.0.6 in the lockfile\n\nTaking package-lock.json from master reverted form-data to 4.0.5. The\nconsolidation carries #834 (form-data 4.0.5 -> 4.0.6, already closed as\nsuperseded), so re-derive it with npm update. It is a transitive of\naxios@1.18.1, whose range is ^4.0.5.\n\n* fix(lint): restore the typescript-eslint eslint-recommended compat layer\n\n`plugin:@typescript-eslint/recommended` in the deleted .eslintrc reached the\n`eslint-recommended` compat layer through `extends`. The flat port spread only\n`tsPlugin.configs.recommended.rules`, so that layer was lost and the core rules\nTypeScript already covers stayed on for .ts files.\n\nReproduced: `src/probe.ts` containing `export const env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv =\nprocess.env` failed with `''NodeJS'' is not defined  no-undef`, and\n`eslint --print-config` showed `no-undef: [2, {typeof: false}]` and\n`no-redeclare: [2, {builtinGlobals: true}]` active. Under master''s .eslintrc\nboth are `off` and the probe exits 0.\n\nFixed with `...tsPlugin.configs[''flat/recommended'']`, which composes base +\neslint-recommended + recommended in the right order and keeps the layer scoped\nto .ts/.tsx/.mts/.cts. `js.configs.recommended` moves up to its own array\nelement so the layer has something to switch off; spreading it into `rules`\nalongside the others is what caused the earlier bug in this file, and that fix\nis preserved.\n\nMeasured on .ts with `eslint --print-config`: 18 core rules go from enabled to\noff (no-undef, no-redeclare, constructor-super, no-const-assign,\nno-dupe-class-members, no-unreachable, no-dupe-keys, ...) and 4 that the layer\nenables and the old spread dropped come on (no-var, prefer-const,\nprefer-rest-params, prefer-spread). On .jsx all 22 keep master''s severity, so\nthe layer does not leak onto JavaScript. The remaining enabled-set differences\nagainst master are all accounted for by the eslint 8->10 and typescript-eslint\n7->8 majors.\n\nAlso in this commit:\n\n- Add `jsx` (and `mts,cts`) to the `files` glob. `src` holds 30 .jsx files,\n  including every `reactApp` component across all six step directories, and\n  they were invisible to `npm run lint`: 44 files linted, all .js. Now 74 files\n  (44 .js + 30 .jsx), still 0 problems, so nothing needed fixing. Verified they\n  were genuinely skipped before, not merely clean: a .jsx probe reports \"File\n  ignored because no matching configuration was supplied\" under the old glob and\n  2 real errors under the new one.\n- Drop `@typescript-eslint/no-var-requires: ''off''`. The rule still exists in\n  typescript-eslint 8 but is deprecated since 8.0.0 and is not in `recommended`,\n  so the line was inert; line 44''s `no-require-imports: ''off''` does the work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Luis Villamarin <luis.villamarin@nearform.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"55521650875d36f2154d2e5c1e3f70e15ab41117","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nearform/the-micro-frontends-workshop/git/trees/55521650875d36f2154d2e5c1e3f70e15ab41117"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nearform/the-micro-frontends-workshop/git/commits/6f8fd98acef68def2a51af1252344bcc86f54e7b","verification":{"payload":"tree 55521650875d36f2154d2e5c1e3f70e15ab41117\nparent aaad1be2c45aeba4b8ade19392bb3abfcf09e88e\nauthor lv10 <luisvillamarin@gmail.com> 1787069888 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787069888 -0400\n\nchore(deps): consolidate Dependabot updates (#860)\n\n* chore(deps): consolidate Dependabot updates\n\nFolds all 12 open Dependabot PRs into one change: eslint 8 -> 10 with the .eslintrc ->\nflat config migration, typescript-eslint 7 -> 8 (8.67 rather than 8.48, whose peer range\nexcludes eslint 10), react-router 7.18 and form-data 4.0.6. Five of the PRs were stale.\n\nCloses #859\n\n* chore(deps): restore form-data 4.0.6 in the lockfile\n\nTaking package-lock.json from master reverted form-data to 4.0.5. The\nconsolidation carries #834 (form-data 4.0.5 -> 4.0.6, already closed as\nsuperseded), so re-derive it with npm update. It is a transitive of\naxios@1.18.1, whose range is ^4.0.5.\n\n* fix(lint): restore the typescript-eslint eslint-recommended compat layer\n\n`plugin:@typescript-eslint/recommended` in the deleted .eslintrc reached the\n`eslint-recommended` compat layer through `extends`. The flat port spread only\n`tsPlugin.configs.recommended.rules`, so that layer was lost and the core rules\nTypeScript already covers stayed on for .ts files.\n\nReproduced: `src/probe.ts` containing `export const env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv =\nprocess.env` failed with `''NodeJS'' is not defined  no-undef`, and\n`eslint --print-config` showed `no-undef: [2, {typeof: false}]` and\n`no-redeclare: [2, {builtinGlobals: true}]` active. Under master''s .eslintrc\nboth are `off` and the probe exits 0.\n\nFixed with `...tsPlugin.configs[''flat/recommended'']`, which composes base +\neslint-recommended + recommended in the right order and keeps the layer scoped\nto .ts/.tsx/.mts/.cts. `js.configs.recommended` moves up to its own array\nelement so the layer has something to switch off; spreading it into `rules`\nalongside the others is what caused the earlier bug in this file, and that fix\nis preserved.\n\nMeasured on .ts with `eslint --print-config`: 18 core rules go from enabled to\noff (no-undef, no-redeclare, constructor-super, no-const-assign,\nno-dupe-class-members, no-unreachable, no-dupe-keys, ...) and 4 that the layer\nenables and the old spread dropped come on (no-var, prefer-const,\nprefer-rest-params, prefer-spread). On .jsx all 22 keep master''s severity, so\nthe layer does not leak onto JavaScript. The remaining enabled-set differences\nagainst master are all accounted for by the eslint 8->10 and typescript-eslint\n7->8 majors.\n\nAlso in this commit:\n\n- Add `jsx` (and `mts,cts`) to the `files` glob. `src` holds 30 .jsx files,\n  including every `reactApp` component across all six step directories, and\n  they were invisible to `npm run lint`: 44 files linted, all .js. Now 74 files\n  (44 .js + 30 .jsx), still 0 problems, so nothing needed fixing. Verified they\n  were genuinely skipped before, not merely clean: a .jsx probe reports \"File\n  ignored because no matching configuration was supplied\" under the old glob and\n  2 real errors under the new one.\n- Drop `@typescript-eslint/no-var-requires: ''off''`. The rule still exists in\n  typescript-eslint 8 but is deprecated since 8.0.0 and is not in `recommended`,\n  so the line was inert; line 44''s `no-require-imports: ''off''` does the work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Luis Villamarin <luis.villamarin@nearform.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhIXACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJD4QADPV0a0ueJbe3JF7XA8Owssa\nK4tYSMnP4AxTkO4j15lJ9sXBxQ+FUqzME9W+m2ihookrUI6Mxcp8ntFIOfFlSbKe\n/3wj5dHPtxTsS/5NcXuSiDrSCVQ2cePuNRbqVk9FeYiw+bKcsgRJCnmIxA9OypdD\ntgSbiZMN4/lGfJKlCI7rMJ16ghrk/wBfNQGuS5FRvzrQ8c8F85DwnWLD1MSDNK4+\n/dQwmFcvDMdIvtg5sdLnSKD77TqAViA01dMGgT96kVFj4r9wZnoi7mo1ZpVNyLjm\nj1nFPNt7EkKRIFNGzAN5yiEsKvhX/vd2xgjXvZyE6/PWHd1WMTwgmu7Z9oAW/7AC\nFbA6qjMf2i8w/LdxHzDpe2QmHBxQlQFcN51FMj88+jaOrgihwgBmra+LTiHUIXf0\nfYtElJ/838or/Y6oikY7BvcDHbpuDX1wYf+c5hfkFcY7zUqfT+KB2DIgNLIINlbO\n81lWPKrC+IhU/noUNZyJRQ8atHpJKIFGbwi6ePsVzQgAtxlzNrl1BBY4ko9Je/37\nF5yFRD4FchGmFavH+i5qzH5khNvG4JGjVnexDeFVNdb0fI+9s5ksta9M/7gOsdlz\nC2XJhUE2ndyGfihrDJTcUfOm14RwRpwoXCSvg8jFRmJe/hzVFpS+WhBvKdNJgjQM\nsYHHEIUlKFm0tjHfkt0M\n=P5dr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T16:18:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nearform/the-micro-frontends-workshop/commit/6f8fd98acef68def2a51af1252344bcc86f54e7b","node_id":"C_kwDOJ6AXQdoAKDZmOGZkOThhY2VmNjhkZWYyYTUxYWYxMjUyMzQ0YmNjODZmNTRlN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nearform/the-micro-frontends-workshop/commit/aaad1be2c45aeba4b8ade19392bb3abfcf09e88e","sha":"aaad1be2c45aeba4b8ade19392bb3abfcf09e88e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nearform/the-micro-frontends-workshop/commits/aaad1be2c45aeba4b8ade19392bb3abfcf09e88e"}],"sha":"6f8fd98acef68def2a51af1252344bcc86f54e7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nearform/the-micro-frontends-workshop/commits/6f8fd98acef68def2a51af1252344bcc86f54e7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/