ProxyServerUrl port against angular.json serve\nports, then to a single-project workspace, and finally to the naming\nconvention and the interactive prompt.\n\nAdd --angular-project to override discovery with an angular.json project\nname or a directory path, and expand --help with per-option descriptions.\n\n* Add provideAppInfo\n\n* Bump version","tree":{"sha":"83ecbbec924641f24bdba451c46e1e9b5de2ee87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g10101k/Oip/git/trees/83ecbbec924641f24bdba451c46e1e9b5de2ee87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g10101k/Oip/git/commits/03e4bffb486fc87d88ecd23552057b43b675ba11","verification":{"payload":"tree 83ecbbec924641f24bdba451c46e1e9b5de2ee87\nparent 200c82c3b1ef45fb5dce622f65b363cb6da98b5f\nauthor Igor Tyulyakov <g101k@mail.ru> 1788465661 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788465661 +0300\n\nDiscover Angular project from SPA proxy properties in CLI (#339)\n\n* Discover Angular project from SPA proxy properties in CLI\n\nReplace the hardcoded backend-to-Angular project map in ProjectResolver\nwith discovery based on SpaRoot, SpaProxyServerUrl and SpaProxyLaunchCommand:\nresolve the npm script from the launch command down to its \"ng serve\" call,\nfall back to matching the SpaProxyServerUrl port against angular.json serve\nports, then to a single-project workspace, and finally to the naming\nconvention and the interactive prompt.\n\nAdd --angular-project to override discovery with an angular.json project\nname or a directory path, and expand --help with per-option descriptions.\n\n* Add provideAppInfo\n\n* Bump version","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmdH9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6XIQAH+xRHWo5QGqNxL9Gv+ot3B3\nhnMwo0o3paKe1gDasLMPIKBY1r+0li3HpmXF1huAiA5g3h9+/8xK9ZS9XG/6bvfa\nqKwsVa25b1ORhEbxWbJK6y69tPgj1vy7sYwlUAoMCX9T6V/FFig8jQW1jAdulpxW\nJxMh92kJctcI6bkAe//Owbh34JELGnwambu+pJzgJm5EoV/Rg5f631AsBYHWz1zQ\n15j2JmJlV9LIexFVOvWQLrQQRJwvCoJXBs/7VaOC6fvfAyJIMVavDgmYIka+Odu0\nzsunFlZ3X19OS1e/5