d":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catastrophe-brandon","id":20647751,"login":"catastrophe-brandon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjQ3NzUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/astro-virtual-assistant-frontend/commits/664463822d3f19e41edfe6f9bcaa90e2a5e41973/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T15:43:12Z","email":"btweed@redhat.com","name":"Brandon Tweed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T15:43:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/add e2e tests (#394)\n\n* feat: add Playwright E2E testing to Konflux pipeline\n\nAdd E2E testing capability using Playwright with sequential execution:\n\nPrerequisites:\n- Install Playwright 1.40.0 (matches auth package requirement)\n- Install @redhat-cloud-services/playwright-test-auth for shared auth logic\n- Add playwright.config.ts with sequential execution (workers: 1, fullyParallel: false)\n- Create example smoke test in playwright/example.spec.ts\n\nPipeline Configuration:\n- Update pipeline to use docker-build-run-all-tests.yaml (from docker-build-oci-ta.yaml)\n- Add workspace-setup-script to install dependencies before tests\n- Add unit-tests-script to run Jest tests (npm run test)\n- Add e2e-tests-script to run Playwright tests (npx playwright test)\n- Add run-app-script to serve app with Caddy\n- Configure e2e-playwright-image: mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.40.0-jammy\n- Reference virtual-assistant-dev-proxy-caddyfile ConfigMap\n- Reference virtual-assistant-credentials-secret ExternalSecret\n\nVersion Alignment:\n- package.json @playwright/test: 1.40.0\n- Auth package requirement: ^1.40.0\n- Docker image: v1.40.0-jammy\nAll three versions aligned for browser compatibility.\n\nDependencies:\n- Requires ConfigMap and ExternalSecret from konflux-release-data MR\n- MR: https://gitlab.cee.redhat.com/releng/konflux-release-data/-/merge_requests/18405\n- DO NOT merge this PR until the above MR is merged and resources are deployed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: update Playwright to 1.60.0 for version alignment\n\n- Update @playwright/test from 1.40.0 to 1.60.0\n- Update playwright from 1.40.0 to 1.60.0\n- Update pipeline Docker image from v1.40.0-jammy to v1.60.0-jammy\n\nThis resolves version mismatch where playwright-test-auth was pulling\nplaywright@1.60.0 while @playwright/test was at 1.40.0.\n\nAll versions now aligned:\n- @playwright/test: 1.60.0\n- playwright: 1.60.0\n- Docker image: v1.60.0-jammy\n\n* fix(pipeline): increase workspace storage from 1Gi to 2Gi\n\nnpm ci was failing with ENOSPC (no space left on device) during\ndependency installation. Using 2Gi instead of 3Gi to avoid\nResourceQuota conflicts while still providing sufficient space\nfor node_modules with Playwright dependencies.\n\nReference: landing-page-frontend uses 2Gi successfully.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(pipeline): migrate to v2 pipeline with envFrom secret management\n\nUpdate pipeline to use docker-build-run-all-tests-v2.yaml which\nprovides flexible secret management via envFrom.\n\nv2 automatically imports all secret keys as environment variables,\nmaking it easier to add custom env vars without modifying the\npipeline definition.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(playwright): update baseURL to use frontend proxy in CI\n\nChange default baseURL from localhost:8004 to stage.foo.redhat.com:1337\nto match the pattern used by all working E2E test repos.\n\nIn CI, the Konflux pipeline runs a frontend proxy sidecar on\nstage.foo.redhat.com:1337 that routes requests to the actual stage\nenvironment based on the ConfigMap routes.\n\nChanges:\n- baseURL: http://localhost:8004 → https://stage.foo.redhat.com:1337\n- Add ignoreHTTPSErrors: true (for self-signed certs in CI proxy)\n\nMatches pattern from:\n- learning-resources\n- frontend-starter-app\n- landing-page-frontend\n- widget-layout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(pipeline): add hostAliases for stage.foo.redhat.com DNS resolution\n\nAdd podTemplate with hostAliases to map stage.foo.redhat.com to localhost.\nThis allows Playwright tests to connect to the frontend-dev-proxy sidecar\nwhich listens on localhost:1337.\n\nWithout this, DNS resolution fails with ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED because\nstage.foo.redhat.com doesn''t exist as a real hostname in the cluster.\n\nThe hostAliases adds /etc/hosts entries:\n- ::1 stage.foo.redhat.com (IPv6)\n- 127.0.0.1 stage.foo.redhat.com (IPv4)\n\nMatches pattern from:\n- learning-resources\n- frontend-starter-app\n- landing-page-frontend\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): remove networkidle wait that causes test timeouts\n\nRemove waitForLoadState(''networkidle'') from smoke test. Apps with\nongoing background activity (polling, websockets, analytics) never\nreach network idle state, causing tests to timeout.\n\nThe default page.goto() behavior (waiting for ''load'' event) is\nsufficient. Tests should wait for specific UI elements instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(e2e): add comprehensive Virtual Assistant interaction test\n\nReplace placeholder smoke test with functional E2E test that validates:\n1. Virtual Assistant is closed on landing page load\n2. Toggle button opens the assistant\n3. Default model selection is \"General Red Hat (Default)\"\n4. Model selection dropdown displays correct selected option\n5. Close button properly closes the assistant\n\nTest uses proper selectors inferred from codebase:\n- Toggle button: button[aria-label=\"Launch AI assistant\"]\n- Chatbot container: #ai-chatbot\n- Model selection: .universal-model-selection__toggle\n- Close button: .pf-chatbot__header-actions button[aria-label*=\"Close\"]\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(e2e): integrate playwright-test-auth for SSO authentication\n\nConfigure Playwright to use the @redhat-cloud-services/playwright-test-auth\npackage for automated Red Hat SSO authentication. This provides:\n\n- Global setup that authenticates once before all tests\n- Shared authentication state across all test runs\n- Automatic handling of SSO login flow\n- Reusable session management\n\nChanges:\n- Added globalSetup from playwright-test-auth to playwright.config.ts\n- Configured storageState to save/load authentication session\n- Added playwright/.auth to .gitignore to prevent committing credentials\n- Updated test documentation to clarify authentication is automatic\n\nAuthentication credentials are provided via E2E_USER and E2E_PASSWORD\nenvironment variables (managed by Konflux pipeline via ExternalSecret).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): use string path for globalSetup instead of function import\n\nPlaywright config requires globalSetup to be a file path string, not a\nfunction reference. Updated to use the correct module path syntax.\n\nError fixed:\n  config.globalSetup must be a string\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): add aria-label to launch button and extend module load timeout\n\nAdded aria-label attribute to UniversalBadge button for better accessibility\nand test reliability. Introduced FEDERATED_MODULE_TIMEOUT constant (15s) to\naccount for asynchronous module federation loading of the Virtual Assistant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(e2e): make test environment-aware and improve close button accessibility\n\n- Added specific aria-label \"Close AI assistant\" to chatbot header close button\n  to distinguish it from banner close button\n- Made Playwright test environment-aware by checking feature flags and ARH\n  authentication to determine expected default assistant\n- Updated test to dynamically expect either \"Ask Red Hat\" or \"Hybrid Cloud Console\"\n  based on environment configuration\n- Updated Cypress test to use new aria-label for consistency\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(e2e): rename and improve test code quality\n\n- Renamed example.spec.ts to e2e.spec.ts for clarity\n- Fixed race condition by setting up response listeners before navigation\n- Improved type safety: replaced ''any'' with proper TypeScript interfaces\n- Extracted selectors into SELECTORS constant for reusability\n- Created detectEnabledAssistants() helper function with JSDoc\n- Added error handling for JSON parsing\n- Fixed step numbering (now sequential 1-6)\n- Used ''as const'' for SELECTORS immutability\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(pipeline): update Playwright version comment from 1.40 to 1.60\n\nFixed outdated comment in Tekton pipeline that referenced Playwright 1.40.0\nwhen the actual version in use is 1.60.0 (matching package.json and the\nplaywright image version).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): use playwright-test-auth disableCookiePrompt to block TrustArc overlay\n\nThe TrustArc cookie consent overlay was blocking clicks in CI. Instead of\nimplementing custom handling, use the built-in disableCookiePrompt function\nfrom @redhat-cloud-services/playwright-test-auth which is specifically\ndesigned to handle this Red Hat console common element.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): properly await API responses in detectEnabledAssistants\n\nFixed race condition where detectEnabledAssistants was returning stale\ndefault values before API responses arrived. The function now:\n\n- Uses page.waitForResponse to wait for actual API responses\n- Properly types Response from @playwright/test\n- Uses API_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT constant instead of hard-coded values\n- Returns actual feature flag and auth status instead of always false\n\nThis ensures the test correctly determines the expected default assistant\nbased on the actual environment configuration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style(e2e): alphabetize imports to satisfy ESLint sort-imports rule\n\nReordered imports from ''@playwright/test'' alphabetically:\n- Before: test, expect, Page, Response\n- After: expect, Page, Response, test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve playwright config and accessibility issues\n\n- Fix globalSetup to use require.resolve() for proper module resolution\n- Fix ARH auth detection to target specific endpoint (/hydra/rest/contacts/sso/current)\n- Fix race condition: call detectEnabledAssistants before navigation, await after\n- Fix duplicate screen reader announcement: use empty alt=\"\" on decorative image\n- Update Cypress tests to match new empty alt attribute\n\nAll changes ensure proper async handling, specific endpoint matching,\nand improved accessibility for assistive technologies.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"925ae01e5d62354d565409d69a655672e836ec05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/astro-virtual-assistant-frontend/git/trees/925ae01e5d62354d565409d69a655672e836ec05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/astro-virtual-assistant-frontend/git/commits/664463822d3f19e41edfe6f9bcaa90e2a5e41973","verification":{"payload":"tree 925ae01e5d62354d565409d69a655672e836ec05\nparent e39e1f26b0cdf43769fb4c80610c28bc06e7a6ba\nauthor Brandon Tweed <btweed@redhat.com> 1780501392 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780501392 -0400\n\nFeat/add e2e tests (#394)\n\n* feat: add Playwright E2E testing to Konflux pipeline\n\nAdd E2E testing capability using Playwright with sequential execution:\n\nPrerequisites:\n- Install Playwright 1.40.0 (matches auth package requirement)\n- Install @redhat-cloud-services/playwright-test-auth for shared auth logic\n- Add playwright.config.ts with sequential execution (workers: 1, fullyParallel: false)\n- Create example smoke test in playwright/example.spec.ts\n\nPipeline Configuration:\n- Update pipeline to use docker-build-run-all-tests.yaml (from docker-build-oci-ta.yaml)\n- Add workspace-setup-script to install dependencies before tests\n- Add unit-tests-script to run Jest tests (npm run test)\n- Add e2e-tests-script to run Playwright tests (npx playwright test)\n- Add run-app-script to serve app with Caddy\n- Configure e2e-playwright-image: mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.40.0-jammy\n- Reference virtual-assistant-dev-proxy-caddyfile ConfigMap\n- Reference virtual-assistant-credentials-secret ExternalSecret\n\nVersion Alignment:\n- package.json @playwright/test: 1.40.0\n- Auth package requirement: ^1.40.0\n- Docker image: v1.40.0-jammy\nAll three versions aligned for browser compatibility.\n\nDependencies:\n- Requires ConfigMap and ExternalSecret from konflux-release-data MR\n- MR: https://gitlab.cee.redhat.com/releng/konflux-release-data/-/merge_requests/18405\n- DO NOT merge this PR until the above MR is merged and resources are deployed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: update Playwright to 1.60.0 for version alignment\n\n- Update @playwright/test from 1.40.0 to 1.60.0\n- Update playwright from 1.40.0 to 1.60.0\n- Update pipeline Docker image from v1.40.0-jammy to v1.60.0-jammy\n\nThis resolves version mismatch where playwright-test-auth was pulling\nplaywright@1.60.0 while @playwright/test was at 1.40.0.\n\nAll versions now aligned:\n- @playwright/test: 1.60.0\n- playwright: 1.60.0\n- Docker image: v1.60.0-jammy\n\n* fix(pipeline): increase workspace storage from 1Gi to 2Gi\n\nnpm ci was failing with ENOSPC (no space left on device) during\ndependency installation. Using 2Gi instead of 3Gi to avoid\nResourceQuota conflicts while still providing sufficient space\nfor node_modules with Playwright dependencies.\n\nReference: landing-page-frontend uses 2Gi successfully.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(pipeline): migrate to v2 pipeline with envFrom secret management\n\nUpdate pipeline to use docker-build-run-all-tests-v2.yaml which\nprovides flexible secret management via envFrom.\n\nv2 automatically imports all secret keys as environment variables,\nmaking it easier to add custom env vars without modifying the\npipeline definition.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(playwright): update baseURL to use frontend proxy in CI\n\nChange default baseURL from localhost:8004 to stage.foo.redhat.com:1337\nto match the pattern used by all working E2E test repos.\n\nIn CI, the Konflux pipeline runs a frontend proxy sidecar on\nstage.foo.redhat.com:1337 that routes requests to the actual stage\nenvironment based on the ConfigMap routes.\n\nChanges:\n- baseURL: http://localhost:8004 → https://stage.foo.redhat.com:1337\n- Add ignoreHTTPSErrors: true (for self-signed certs in CI proxy)\n\nMatches pattern from:\n- learning-resources\n- frontend-starter-app\n- landing-page-frontend\n- widget-layout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(pipeline): add hostAliases for stage.foo.redhat.com DNS resolution\n\nAdd podTemplate with hostAliases to map stage.foo.redhat.com to localhost.\nThis allows Playwright tests to connect to the frontend-dev-proxy sidecar\nwhich listens on localhost:1337.\n\nWithout this, DNS resolution fails with ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED because\nstage.foo.redhat.com doesn''t exist as a real hostname in the cluster.\n\nThe hostAliases adds /etc/hosts entries:\n- ::1 stage.foo.redhat.com (IPv6)\n- 127.0.0.1 stage.foo.redhat.com (IPv4)\n\nMatches pattern from:\n- learning-resources\n- frontend-starter-app\n- landing-page-frontend\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): remove networkidle wait that causes test timeouts\n\nRemove waitForLoadState(''networkidle'') from smoke test. Apps with\nongoing background activity (polling, websockets, analytics) never\nreach network idle state, causing tests to timeout.\n\nThe default page.goto() behavior (waiting for ''load'' event) is\nsufficient. Tests should wait for specific UI elements instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(e2e): add comprehensive Virtual Assistant interaction test\n\nReplace placeholder smoke test with functional E2E test that validates:\n1. Virtual Assistant is closed on landing page load\n2. Toggle button opens the assistant\n3. Default model selection is \"General Red Hat (Default)\"\n4. Model selection dropdown displays correct selected option\n5. Close button properly closes the assistant\n\nTest uses proper selectors inferred from codebase:\n- Toggle button: button[aria-label=\"Launch AI assistant\"]\n- Chatbot container: #ai-chatbot\n- Model selection: .universal-model-selection__toggle\n- Close button: .pf-chatbot__header-actions button[aria-label*=\"Close\"]\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(e2e): integrate playwright-test-auth for SSO authentication\n\nConfigure Playwright to use the @redhat-cloud-services/playwright-test-auth\npackage for automated Red Hat SSO authentication. This provides:\n\n- Global setup that authenticates once before all tests\n- Shared authentication state across all test runs\n- Automatic handling of SSO login flow\n- Reusable session management\n\nChanges:\n- Added globalSetup from playwright-test-auth to playwright.config.ts\n- Configured storageState to save/load authentication session\n- Added playwright/.auth to .gitignore to prevent committing credentials\n- Updated test documentation to clarify authentication is automatic\n\nAuthentication credentials are provided via E2E_USER and E2E_PASSWORD\nenvironment variables (managed by Konflux pipeline via ExternalSecret).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): use string path for globalSetup instead of function import\n\nPlaywright config requires globalSetup to be a file path string, not a\nfunction reference. Updated to use the correct module path syntax.\n\nError fixed:\n  config.globalSetup must be a string\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): add aria-label to launch button and extend module load timeout\n\nAdded aria-label attribute to UniversalBadge button for better accessibility\nand test reliability. Introduced FEDERATED_MODULE_TIMEOUT constant (15s) to\naccount for asynchronous module federation loading of the Virtual Assistant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(e2e): make test environment-aware and improve close button accessibility\n\n- Added specific aria-label \"Close AI assistant\" to chatbot header close button\n  to distinguish it from banner close button\n- Made Playwright test environment-aware by checking feature flags and ARH\n  authentication to determine expected default assistant\n- Updated test to dynamically expect either \"Ask Red Hat\" or \"Hybrid Cloud Console\"\n  based on environment configuration\n- Updated Cypress test to use new aria-label for consistency\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(e2e): rename and improve test code quality\n\n- Renamed example.spec.ts to e2e.spec.ts for clarity\n- Fixed race condition by setting up response listeners before navigation\n- Improved type safety: replaced ''any'' with proper TypeScript interfaces\n- Extracted selectors into SELECTORS constant for reusability\n- Created detectEnabledAssistants() helper function with JSDoc\n- Added error handling for JSON parsing\n- Fixed step numbering (now sequential 1-6)\n- Used ''as const'' for SELECTORS immutability\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(pipeline): update Playwright version comment from 1.40 to 1.60\n\nFixed outdated comment in Tekton pipeline that referenced Playwright 1.40.0\nwhen the actual version in use is 1.60.0 (matching package.json and the\nplaywright image version).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): use playwright-test-auth disableCookiePrompt to block TrustArc overlay\n\nThe TrustArc cookie consent overlay was blocking clicks in CI. Instead of\nimplementing custom handling, use the built-in disableCookiePrompt function\nfrom @redhat-cloud-services/playwright-test-auth which is specifically\ndesigned to handle this Red Hat console common element.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): properly await API responses in detectEnabledAssistants\n\nFixed race condition where detectEnabledAssistants was returning stale\ndefault values before API responses arrived. The function now:\n\n- Uses page.waitForResponse to wait for actual API responses\n- Properly types Response from @playwright/test\n- Uses API_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT constant instead of hard-coded values\n- Returns actual feature flag and auth status instead of always false\n\nThis ensures the test correctly determines the expected default assistant\nbased on the actual environment configuration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style(e2e): alphabetize imports to satisfy ESLint sort-imports rule\n\nReordered imports from ''@playwright/test'' alphabetically:\n- Before: test, expect, Page, Response\n- After: expect, Page, Response, test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve playwright config and accessibility issues\n\n- Fix globalSetup to use require.resolve() for proper module resolution\n- Fix ARH auth detection to target specific endpoint (/hydra/rest/contacts/sso/current)\n- Fix race condition: call detectEnabledAssistants before navigation, await after\n- Fix duplicate screen reader announcement: use empty alt=\"\" on decorative image\n- Update Cypress tests to match new empty alt attribute\n\nAll changes ensure proper async handling, specific endpoint matching,\nand improved accessibility for assistive technologies.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIEuQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+vIQAAM3RmSZgQTbRG69JugZH38c\n+4zjKtLt6sgx+WaQm2WLkKCyzVF9QpDUGtK3EZQCStCb95bioyzlt3IC6vB78eiE\niv9C1HEeJhPfFn6sCEQADEB7BHiHZ+R4XfeVAoY6sLLOy5MJGdxOJKwdgI00UTyq\ncS4bNTCqAldZ1dOQqcSxe7m0bQlsoF5vlaUd7Uf0FSKbQTTk+SUnHhCnJCtLSOUH\n9SrATMqG/gQF1tXOllIn7x9NWOnbfgCMDFmF5mIQZcYEhINjE8Jh8/XkRi4Pk65M\nmeTdhUEKeOiVgGfMoP2cwqSR+G2l5eeZTpL5evbYpxErfAR8Kf3lDPvLYaoYvrwG\n9bTH2Ib99aXJbU3h4AVbHawQV0i2xBtUjOkPBs5lk0ChHtG1mTQRafL6imT9p8DW\ny++KbWFo6BfOZgCV9z99rTkoBCMh4VNxxBriH79C+G015xV5O+94XjW8o+meQNO4\nuGjzavV3+Slxtp/tKDzMwUKzm4GFISOXUMtZQzDcVLD78Y24eIlcEzqRckm/gK9e\n+sGxTs/ElbpQKEo0BBQJY3ZPDFadFQu4nwkGeIZwacPX63k7UnexfefACl4Dguoz\n6SMwHzvIHHHL+fKA6pHMldWdR9lc6Tpn55M0z7ESeWXyiLAX4tmssD9AO2Mk4RXj\nNhn3Wy00zpivKh7FV9sS\n=loqV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-03T15:43:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","grav