0-08T18:10:32.624Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22185362?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv","id":22185362,"login":"IanOliv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg1MzYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/7e22f3c6383fd1e8700fddea2328970de56e4266/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T06:08:29Z","email":"22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T06:08:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(nav): hide a manifest module from nav without its permission (#21)\n\nA remote''s manifest entry can now name a nav.requiredPermission\n(\"resource:action\"), checked against the signed-in user''s session\npermissions before the module shows up in the rail/bottom bar/⌘K —\nsigned-out counts as lacking it. chat_remote now declares ai:chat.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0af6baeab5cab72442c361fdcc9d9719d7b9251e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/trees/0af6baeab5cab72442c361fdcc9d9719d7b9251e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/commits/7e22f3c6383fd1e8700fddea2328970de56e4266","verification":{"payload":"tree 0af6baeab5cab72442c361fdcc9d9719d7b9251e\nparent 82c5fd7947f8cdc47644954f2e8a1401c3b7993a\nauthor Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa <22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790575709 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790575709 -0300\n\nfeat(nav): hide a manifest module from nav without its permission (#21)\n\nA remote''s manifest entry can now name a nav.requiredPermission\n(\"resource:action\"), checked against the signed-in user''s session\npermissions before the module shows up in the rail/bottom bar/⌘K —\nsigned-out counts as lacking it. chat_remote now declares ai:chat.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqugRdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc3sQABKzYD6naF1/taSpVrXPyNrN\n7OKUN5ijpx0qyN9URoBcxuQNhUwSLeJt8O/LVY3JuT2v2VIDAsabaAxnQRnthIGB\ncImXQcxjZcPcZV6ukdL5eel4BV9gpGZC2m8N1oy/dFc8JKtyIZMKq01hzxGgkhcR\nIvXxg13ILrLvfnIwLK8YjRq8pWYm8GVqAc2YNfr4Dm3xw2Wf4C9dJl5bBNfJcIu5\n9HwWwyoIZoM0MzBrnITjjMCvQWPRdVy7xyIVEV5WcTW6v/fNoQxE2gDqCdOs00l9\nJ/ncnIBqI+SI+FuVsOFLlXNGlI0a7VsebOREuDAVbqDR12DBFckeC7fLVSShWgwn\n+zuwlljv5zF2VWthBZD6dXFclEJqh4xZGPy30zvlh8yayFGcPk3Bd/+Mnm0c1cia\nGXp4lsrxiQCFdKgPaPKUwWrFdVE40uHMUcuwbl2X++kb/yhBiWqwU94Wy8aK/0JU\n0pi8SAi8txtSgGirkCQj4liO8jNRFwvTZWU93O1LWArsBEGylTL4djNdq7BujGlH\nQwZi5pNpQ/IMwSSNze4qNV8wBcVylQ+5EgoDyrWuqCzlLfb0JH2faWa06APOH0Nb\nAgKFoXH4rQHireDj8g1kHXSjUDAnq1+vfJWcer5CIuTeNzuSO/qpA6NEacWijv0R\nhweC16eqSrRQly3Ve9eq\n=GZCA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T06:08:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/7e22f3c6383fd1e8700fddea2328970de56e4266","node_id":"C_kwDOKB7Fj9oAKDdlMjJmM2M2MzgzZmQxZTg3MDBmZGRlYTIzMjg5NzBkZTU2ZTQyNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/82c5fd7947f8cdc47644954f2e8a1401c3b7993a","sha":"82c5fd7947f8cdc47644954f2e8a1401c3b7993a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/82c5fd7947f8cdc47644954f2e8a1401c3b7993a"}],"sha":"7e22f3c6383fd1e8700fddea2328970de56e4266","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/7e22f3c6383fd1e8700fddea2328970de56e4266"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22185362?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv","id":22185362,"login":"IanOliv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg1MzYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/82c5fd7947f8cdc47644954f2e8a1401c3b7993a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:19:46Z","email":"22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:19:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(remotes): pass the session token through to federated remotes (#20)\n\n* feat(remotes): pass the session token through to federated remotes\n\nExtends HostRemoteProps with an optional token, and DynamicModule now\npasses session.token alongside theme/userProfile — same rule as those\ntwo: a plain prop across the federation boundary, never a shared\nstore. Without a token (signed out), it''s simply undefined and a\nremote falls back to whatever it does in that case (chat_remote, for\none, runs in local-only mode with no backend calls).\n\nThis is what lets chat_remote (ingredient-chat) call wrapper-api''s ai\nworker on the signed-in user''s behalf — see\n0xHackerSpace/ingredient-chat#1.\n\nVerified end-to-end for real: logged in as an existing wrapper-api\nuser, opened /modules/chat, started a new conversation and sent a\nmessage through the actual host + federated remote + wrapper-api\nstack, and got back a real Workers AI reply.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix(hotkeys): guard against keydown events with no event.key\n\nSome synthetic keydown events (browser extensions, autofill, certain\nIME/mobile keyboards) don''t set `key`, and calling .toLowerCase() on\nit crashed the whole app whenever one reached the global ⌘K listener.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"33d27a8b7f91b13bb949d32a81becfbb1f215532","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/trees/33d27a8b7f91b13bb949d32a81becfbb1f215532"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/commits/82c5fd7947f8cdc47644954f2e8a1401c3b7993a","verification":{"payload":"tree 33d27a8b7f91b13bb949d32a81becfbb1f215532\nparent 5e19505b2ff5093d0a6f16fda1b4b64178b13521\nauthor Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa <22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790569186 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790569186 -0300\n\nfeat(remotes): pass the session token through to federated remotes (#20)\n\n* feat(remotes): pass the session token through to federated remotes\n\nExtends HostRemoteProps with an optional token, and DynamicModule now\npasses session.token alongside theme/userProfile — same rule as those\ntwo: a plain prop across the federation boundary, never a shared\nstore. Without a token (signed out), it''s simply undefined and a\nremote falls back to whatever it does in that case (chat_remote, for\none, runs in local-only mode with no backend calls).\n\nThis is what lets chat_remote (ingredient-chat) call wrapper-api''s ai\nworker on the signed-in user''s behalf — see\n0xHackerSpace/ingredient-chat#1.\n\nVerified end-to-end for real: logged in as an existing wrapper-api\nuser, opened /modules/chat, started a new conversation and sent a\nmessage through the actual host + federated remote + wrapper-api\nstack, and got back a real Workers AI reply.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix(hotkeys): guard against keydown events with no event.key\n\nSome synthetic keydown events (browser extensions, autofill, certain\nIME/mobile keyboards) don''t set `key`, and calling .toLowerCase() on\nit crashed the whole app whenever one reached the global ⌘K listener.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueriCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdfgQAFjJzDZsKsAml6baSAzKliwt\n7FaD2j6TaWcIFAhCFGErTR9IzcX4F6aRf7HIrLofcsQXJkjex7Jo2gdCRM8B4jzR\nklWZx9FEBHFtP7GhvFw8Xre1AUjQGyHMLbcz5VHZmX8trY328PY2aHONV4T5e9VU\ndw+SbjFZNS/w39y2h6bOrh1oOBCXnpLmQnIZmPprR8MU2DwX3G40QPKX6qzwnADy\nudV8ey0YKILmAdjT97vRnPkoyWk+MDHMQbVvjP+sAbV2JP7T7yTE/EHDzah58qvL\ngF/9dSGzGUOsIYzE//LlLeBCa7TYPj1wfzZ9NcOV+9SyygLXdLT4xiZv6bNOryBq\nvKcSUc6yVXR3ZplFO9IWonVCXwqK87SpMiiwPRcZvTRXxUL5LT7GKNXokC1Y0Tc0\n3AmEorlA7eKmvnk/OJGxkB6u+ObmnJMrMauCFdZD8brgimA9s1FPlQ6Q9pGeBbsN\nETKgT6TfCsFbp0RDO3YT44X0M8iHEa/cRKcvQo60ddtX4sH/u/UiHpT9/1miUk80\nRw0giWvqLNyZoksYMDnRMu79I6wWo9S7dqtiaR26oDE1PZz7Y7EnefXsY8Hz47qR\nfvkXep5ks75yuHADDPOf8VVmNiBEpuFpyeF74OOoMwoRrry3wUQzN8hBtajWi24d\n2sKEhj/byS3V8g4gR0Oc\n=Asja\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T04:19:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/82c5fd7947f8cdc47644954f2e8a1401c3b7993a","node_id":"C_kwDOKB7Fj9oAKDgyYzVmZDc5NDdmOGNkYzQ3NjQ0OTU0ZjJlOGExNDAxYzNiNzk5M2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/5e19505b2ff5093d0a6f16fda1b4b64178b13521","sha":"5e19505b2ff5093d0a6f16fda1b4b64178b13521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/5e19505b2ff5093d0a6f16fda1b4b64178b13521"}],"sha":"82c5fd7947f8cdc47644954f2e8a1401c3b7993a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/82c5fd7947f8cdc47644954f2e8a1401c3b7993a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22185362?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv","id":22185362,"login":"IanOliv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg1MzYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/5e19505b2ff5093d0a6f16fda1b4b64178b13521/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T01:09:52Z","email":"22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T01:09:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(profile): rebuild the Profile page around the real session (#19)\n\n* feat(profile): rebuild the Profile page around the real session\n\nReplace the leftover deck/card-styled scaffolding (hardcoded green/olive\nbackgrounds, a raw <button>, rendering profile as an array with fields\nthat never matched the real API) with a proper MUI layout that actually\nreflects what login now gives us:\n\n- Signed-out visitors get a \"sign in\" prompt instead of a blank page.\n- Shows the real username/email and role chips from session.profiles\n  (falls back to \"No role assigned\" for freshly self-registered users,\n  since signup grants no default permissions).\n- Session expiry from the login response, plus a \"verified by the\n  server\" checkmark once GET /profile succeeds.\n- The RBAC \"Missing required permission: api:access\" a role-less user\n  gets back is now shown as a plain-language hint instead of raw API\n  text.\n- Sign out lives on the page itself, not just the account menu.\n\nAlso renamed pages/Profile/Chat.tsx -> Profile.tsx (copy-paste leftover\nfrom the old Chat page template) and deleted components/User/Profile/\nstyled.ts, which nothing else used.\n\nVerified with Playwright against a real login flow (dev + prod build):\nsigned-out prompt, real user data after login, role-less permission\nhint, sign-out clearing the session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix(auth): login''s permissions/profiles are objects, not strings\n\nwrapper-api''s POST /login response returns permissions/profiles as the\nraw D1 rows (e.g. profiles: [{id, name, description}]) — only the JWT\npayload embedded in the token flattens them to \"resource:action\"/name\nstrings. LoginResponse/WrapperSession typed both as string[], which\nwas wrong and went uncaught because every test login so far was a\nfresh signup (always empty arrays either way).\n\nReproduced for real: logging in as an account with actual profiles\nassigned crashed the whole app shell with React error #31 (\"objects\nare not valid as a React child\") — Profile''s role chips were handing\na {id, name, description} object straight to a Chip''s label/key, and\nDynamicModule''s session.profiles?.[0] fed the same object into the\nfederated remote''s userProfile prop where a string is expected.\n\nFixed both call sites (Profile''s chips use profile.name/profile.id,\nDynamicModule reads profile.name) and the AuthPermission/AuthProfile\ntypes to match the real shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb0ed2296dc4f1843969c3f72e97f4c1b59f39de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/trees/eb0ed2296dc4f1843969c3f72e97f4c1b59f39de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/commits/5e19505b2ff5093d0a6f16fda1b4b64178b13521","verification":{"payload":"tree eb0ed2296dc4f1843969c3f72e97f4c1b59f39de\nparent e2dbf5b69bb6df5d9da79487e1fbaa8dccd80d9c\nauthor Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa <22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790557792 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790557792 -0300\n\nfeat(profile): rebuild the Profile page around the real session (#19)\n\n* feat(profile): rebuild the Profile page around the real session\n\nReplace the leftover deck/card-styled scaffolding (hardcoded green/olive\nbackgrounds, a raw <button>, rendering profile as an array with fields\nthat never matched the real API) with a proper MUI layout that actually\nreflects what login now gives us:\n\n- Signed-out visitors get a \"sign in\" prompt instead of a blank page.\n- Shows the real username/email and role chips from session.profiles\n  (falls back to \"No role assigned\" for freshly self-registered users,\n  since signup grants no default permissions).\n- Session expiry from the login response, plus a \"verified by the\n  server\" checkmark once GET /profile succeeds.\n- The RBAC \"Missing required permission: api:access\" a role-less user\n  gets back is now shown as a plain-language hint instead of raw API\n  text.\n- Sign out lives on the page itself, not just the account menu.\n\nAlso renamed pages/Profile/Chat.tsx -> Profile.tsx (copy-paste leftover\nfrom the old Chat page template) and deleted components/User/Profile/\nstyled.ts, which nothing else used.\n\nVerified with Playwright against a real login flow (dev + prod build):\nsigned-out prompt, real user data after login, role-less permission\nhint, sign-out clearing the session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix(auth): login''s permissions/profiles are objects, not strings\n\nwrapper-api''s POST /login response returns permissions/profiles as the\nraw D1 rows (e.g. profiles: [{id, name, description}]) — only the JWT\npayload embedded in the token flattens them to \"resource:action\"/name\nstrings. LoginResponse/WrapperSession typed both as string[], which\nwas wrong and went uncaught because every test login so far was a\nfresh signup (always empty arrays either way).\n\nReproduced for real: logging in as an account with actual profiles\nassigned crashed the whole app shell with React error #31 (\"objects\nare not valid as a React child\") — Profile''s role chips were handing\na {id, name, description} object straight to a Chip''s label/key, and\nDynamicModule''s session.profiles?.[0] fed the same object into the\nfederated remote''s userProfile prop where a string is expected.\n\nFixed both call sites (Profile''s chips use profile.name/profile.id,\nDynamicModule reads profile.name) and the AuthPermission/AuthProfile\ntypes to match the real shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqub5gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy1MQAKulWCapZe7uBcm7DAiGSKcG\n3fLELYgzZPlnf2I/1yi74BL/YRrGlEaLVSmORUvCQsECRd3pT2NPLRXirPd+goNi\nPa0QHWkpZxxcIGfF9/KZKFPOBRzgTQmpK3kRDt8Sjf6pg07mznA0cXLTMX2Ar8Uk\nkSXVYWfMzsc1Wa2NaelVpesIicj4MnVEYbSpCZMVhcpJze4X7AzxiMmm/wO7ay3i\nPg7ir6DYiH35aUZff5wrdNEIV0EZ6pyQ/KrxP+2Ozq/E39s7ZZqBFE+sc67EUrnX\nXGoo3I5bfYoP7mEBUg5cLTmkesSHoYoWblzsYtfDFxjPYO2SfHNnp3LGIhTsWwfZ\nEpX6ow3RjYiYYw+ZHTEHNos9wUZhKqInbfftPqawI3No0lAfiBKaBM+FBJM0AD/J\n5tUWHWyGcJFt+8qSk3t3iZWo3SEtO2+Z/AIL9+8BTaG5I5gpbqm12o24qtB+53Tp\nbsy5PzK6LLOh76PMzKDkMrT9xvPWemL8YeA2v+22nDFZ/lkmSyzjuIkB0hduttSo\ne08+VjffFbq58sEZUF5EoKzsvRYPpeJ9ve5W0JZd/TqHNaHUYvK5WXgmx3jSxKHA\n+VlaNcGmznFq14yOMUW228iuaTO/ydyG95IZm3ggIGzil7wMd0sd1qdg7lx3BMhK\nOjaUAl2Nw4J6jJydEo/8\n=09XW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T01:09:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/5e19505b2ff5093d0a6f16fda1b4b64178b13521","node_id":"C_kwDOKB7Fj9oAKDVlMTk1MDViMmZmNTA5M2QwYTZmMTZmZGExYjRiNjQxNzhiMTM1MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/e2dbf5b69bb6df5d9da79487e1fbaa8dccd80d9c","sha":"e2dbf5b69bb6df5d9da79487e1fbaa8dccd80d9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/e2dbf5b69bb6df5d9da79487e1fbaa8dccd80d9c"}],"sha":"5e19505b2ff5093d0a6f16fda1b4b64178b13521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/5e19505b2ff5093d0a6f16fda1b4b64178b13521"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22185362?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv","id":22185362,"login":"IanOliv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg1MzYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/e2dbf5b69bb6df5d9da79487e1fbaa8dccd80d9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T21:58:10Z","email":"22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T21:58:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(auth): wire login, signup and profile to the real wrapper-api (#18)\n\nReplace the never-functional PostgREST-flavored mock client\n(utils/micro/api.ts, hitting a hardcoded localhost:3000 that never\nexisted) with a real client against the wrapper-api auth worker\n(login/signup) and API worker (/profile), both JWT-based.\n\n- New src/utils/auth/{api,types}.ts: login, signup, refreshSession,\n  fetchProfile. Hosts come from VITE_AUTH_API_URL/VITE_WRAPPER_API_URL\n  env vars, never hardcoded — throws clearly if either is unset.\n- store/session: real shape (user, permissions, profiles, refreshToken,\n  expiresAt instead of the old fake role/tenant_name profile), and the\n  session now actually persists to localStorage (was in-memory only,\n  a known rough edge) and clears it on sign out.\n- Login/Register now call the real endpoints instead of doLogin/\n  doRegister''s dead PostgREST RPC shape; Register gains the email\n  field the real signup endpoint requires.\n- Profile fetches the real GET /profile with the session token\n  instead of a hardcoded fetch(''http://localhost:3000/profile''), and\n  no longer refetches on every render (missing effect deps).\n- DynamicModule''s federated-remote profile prop now derives `role`\n  from the real session.profiles[0] instead of a fully mocked object\n  (tenantName stays a placeholder — the backend has no tenant concept).\n\nRequires a matching fix in wrapper-api (0xHackerSpace/wrapper-api#16)\nadding CORS to the auth/api workers — without it, browsers block the\ncross-origin requests even though curl works fine.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"72700563acdc5cb235b8a5cbd56fe2d097b8ed5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/trees/72700563acdc5cb235b8a5cbd56fe2d097b8ed5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/commits/e2dbf5b69bb6df5d9da79487e1fbaa8dccd80d9c","verification":{"payload":"tree 72700563acdc5cb235b8a5cbd56fe2d097b8ed5d\nparent ac39f81f92560058cbe6c76251dca2307786809c\nauthor Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa <22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790546290 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790546290 -0300\n\nfeat(auth): wire login, signup and profile to the real wrapper-api (#18)\n\nReplace the never-functional PostgREST-flavored mock client\n(utils/micro/api.ts, hitting a hardcoded localhost:3000 that never\nexisted) with a real client against the wrapper-api auth worker\n(login/signup) and API worker (/profile), both JWT-based.\n\n- New src/utils/auth/{api,types}.ts: login, signup, refreshSession,\n  fetchProfile. Hosts come from VITE_AUTH_API_URL/VITE_WRAPPER_API_URL\n  env vars, never hardcoded — throws clearly if either is unset.\n- store/session: real shape (user, permissions, profiles, refreshToken,\n  expiresAt instead of the old fake role/tenant_name profile), and the\n  session now actually persists to localStorage (was in-memory only,\n  a known rough edge) and clears it on sign out.\n- Login/Register now call the real endpoints instead of doLogin/\n  doRegister''s dead PostgREST RPC shape; Register gains the email\n  field the real signup endpoint requires.\n- Profile fetches the real GET /profile with the session token\n  instead of a hardcoded fetch(''http://localhost:3000/profile''), and\n  no longer refetches on every render (missing effect deps).\n- DynamicModule''s federated-remote profile prop now derives `role`\n  from the real session.profiles[0] instead of a fully mocked object\n  (tenantName stays a placeholder — the backend has no tenant concept).\n\nRequires a matching fix in wrapper-api (0xHackerSpace/wrapper-api#16)\nadding CORS to the auth/api workers — without it, browsers block the\ncross-origin requests even though curl works fine.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquZFyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjYUQAKdmvBF6sfTkhE6XC0xAI+Wg\nro5kQ4NhYtmUSmmW+JqhGAmyrmBz/YVl5PCEQPZl+ylTg9xIryohKtD4IQgnPzib\nBwXUhGDRZTdNF4BFO/1ws2wK6Ubn0GP+EnfYwfLY1NQWIbJdVRElRlEnH86cw97C\n53BQRY5nD7kWOybC5nN6ZfgK+6q8FKEA2qgm3qjg+l4lVNrQ++GkR/3ekFyAJASM\n7e9zmZKZfMWHLLkySlx+HX5OjdhjgbdIPo9Gh/dv6toZ4peE9zSk1Cftjd1vhQx2\nzxo6bnSY6W5qQD/AM3PlMLwd7XJ8yGsVYOYaQ/E2LOhJR3cqVIPaOS/lx3e00hMT\nXaGwJ5yv9iRSGJqfFWS6u6eQ5XLHPDd83+5hQW3uUz2NgCFQIpxugv03Klva37Pd\nMXpS29mJjez+dKWIzbSujfp71kgnZIaZsEijdGEg086m+EF58H9U8aWg+Hdu85Yw\n7EprLE4K3X5V0XyKrgX8Tty+Ts7EIQHUFJzkKgu8erYKRt3WvuV1ZyORiwEp8PZg\njS9Mcs1Ufli9CmgFOJBJ9VBLc0qJDKKPrFlDeCpbYNZVEJX9hQd4BnI0g+lFDOMB\n8yfSL+gjBNBrrDx6BlRf1XuBc37crrWmrKvvfBDkvEasN2JP4o23EO7T/WcQrVGX\nUZNAC+z+aa3vOudqSBP+\n=QfTo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T21:58:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/e2dbf5b69bb6df5d9da79487e1fbaa8dccd80d9c","node_id":"C_kwDOKB7Fj9oAKGUyZGJmNWI2OWJiNmRmNWQ5ZGE3OTQ4N2UxZmJhYThkY2NkODBkOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/ac39f81f92560058cbe6c76251dca2307786809c","sha":"ac39f81f92560058cbe6c76251dca2307786809c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/ac39f81f92560058cbe6c76251dca2307786809c"}],"sha":"e2dbf5b69bb6df5d9da79487e1fbaa8dccd80d9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/e2dbf5b69bb6df5d9da79487e1fbaa8dccd80d9c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22185362?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv","id":22185362,"login":"IanOliv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg1MzYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/ac39f81f92560058cbe6c76251dca2307786809c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:24:12Z","email":"22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:24:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(host): remove chat-remote app from the monorepo (#17)\n\n* chore(host): remove chat-remote app from the monorepo\n\nThe Chat federated remote now lives in its own repo\n(0xHackerSpace/ingredient-chat), deployed independently to\ningredient-chat.vercel.app. Drop apps/chat-remote and the\nworkspace scripts/deps that only existed to build and run it.\n\nThe host''s manifest-driven remote loading is untouched — only the\nlocal dev manifest''s entry URL now points at the deployed\ningredient-chat instead of a local chat-remote dev server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* chore: retrigger checks after removing wrapper-chat-remote project\n\nEmpty commit to get a fresh status check run now that the orphaned\nwrapper-chat-remote Vercel project (Root Directory apps/chat-remote,\nwhich no longer exists) has been deleted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fbded21bfadd187d0b227db2d0f4420e6ffcf3e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/trees/fbded21bfadd187d0b227db2d0f4420e6ffcf3e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/commits/ac39f81f92560058cbe6c76251dca2307786809c","verification":{"payload":"tree fbded21bfadd187d0b227db2d0f4420e6ffcf3e7\nparent aa47887308010f065e9f19d8656d600edad0d384\nauthor Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa <22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790537052 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790537052 -0300\n\nchore(host): remove chat-remote app from the monorepo (#17)\n\n* chore(host): remove chat-remote app from the monorepo\n\nThe Chat federated remote now lives in its own repo\n(0xHackerSpace/ingredient-chat), deployed independently to\ningredient-chat.vercel.app. Drop apps/chat-remote and the\nworkspace scripts/deps that only existed to build and run it.\n\nThe host''s manifest-driven remote loading is untouched — only the\nlocal dev manifest''s entry URL now points at the deployed\ningredient-chat instead of a local chat-remote dev server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* chore: retrigger checks after removing wrapper-chat-remote project\n\nEmpty commit to get a fresh status check run now that the orphaned\nwrapper-chat-remote Vercel project (Root Directory apps/chat-remote,\nwhich no longer exists) has been deleted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquW1cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAh1MQAC92mE8fv6vBfjcf+TmAn13k\nEkNTxKCzoSLyf0s/KRvOa8FOK5VH5Y8Tjk091zswsRvC7GjZw5H+SVbutdH8YGt5\nIkrRtIiuV6Nb1Bc+RigBltcrhfYUwueLYZmSg1c50QCy6cmIMEZH0eECxrfBg24j\nhbN2vvie+N11xlWR5Pnzm1PwN8HDH0ckZPBr88x3PsO447/gN4N9rFGub7uJPRqm\nIKdqYYkTL+ttpUxvdlW4YVtNuuymp0orK1inDRYcvy9vGLOD9re1BQQqjf2q8VjE\ngjDuQ+w0oME3SIYvmVi9o18mS0KM2vrMG3Pn31oCuFOEmNcbZImqnw2Keshhm8jj\n3cocM8gm9nljwnfJpuuPeaUoiOv0tncvXH9z84J1niGevqS4PmqUWKLlpYjsoRVZ\nR7kWpkVP9IPC7bdH1QRbXpl/Bs8Ks44cXcodwLpNNCHoPzQwxdFZwSyVV9r1YqMj\nRbricpy8tlnQk6NAS9zH8AOW7MGLG7RsHQMuqm+SofxHDeIOWXB8tIqLXvExZTxL\nntg8i8KS9AyyX8R0H9pnIBB+ew3CZ5jb6SM2zvRmFIXfQOs27KwhAzLPeSxbhn2+\nYaunSgQlZRnuAkpqjN21lXwrD2f7b3N4n+cU3Ju/iYKVmiyZDHlFyL2b17cUW6f5\na8v0FrqPwW7VWyBX/HSE\n=gDEc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T19:24:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/ac39f81f92560058cbe6c76251dca2307786809c","node_id":"C_kwDOKB7Fj9oAKGFjMzlmODFmOTI1NjAwNThjYmU2Yzc2MjUxZGNhMjMwNzc4NjgwOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/aa47887308010f065e9f19d8656d600edad0d384","sha":"aa47887308010f065e9f19d8656d600edad0d384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/aa47887308010f065e9f19d8656d600edad0d384"}],"sha":"ac39f81f92560058cbe6c76251dca2307786809c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/ac39f81f92560058cbe6c76251dca2307786809c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22185362?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv","id":22185362,"login":"IanOliv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg1MzYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/aa47887308010f065e9f19d8656d600edad0d384/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:01:40Z","email":"22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:01:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Prototype: Module Federation for the Chat microapp (#7)\n\n* chore: local changes\n\n* feat(federation): federate Chat as a Module Federation remote\n\nRestructures the repo into npm workspaces (apps/host, apps/chat-remote) to\nprototype Module Federation for shared UI components. The Chat microapp is\nextracted into its own independently buildable/deployable package and\nconsumed by the host at runtime via @module-federation/vite.\n\nCross-boundary state (MUI theme, logged-in user profile) is passed as plain\nprops into the exposed component rather than shared as a federation\nsingleton — sharing @mui/material and recoil as singletons hit real bugs in\nthis Rollup/Vite setup (circular init errors, subpath imports bypassing the\nshared scope, and Recoil never actually resolving to the host''s single\ninstance across the boundary).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix(deploy): point Vercel at apps/host/dist\n\nThe app now builds into apps/host/dist after the workspace split, so\nVercel failed with \"No Output Directory named dist found\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* chore(chat-remote): add Vercel headers for cross-origin remote loading\n\nAllows the host to fetch remoteEntry.js and its chunks from another origin\nand keeps remoteEntry.js revalidated so hosts pick up new remote builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* feat(host): make the chat remote URL configurable via CHAT_REMOTE_URL\n\nDefaults to http://localhost:5174 for local dev; set it in the build\nenvironment (Vercel) to point the host at a deployed remote.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* feat(federation): consume remotes from a runtime manifest, not vite.config.ts\n\nGeneralizes Module Federation from one hardcoded remote (chat_remote) to N\nremotes discovered at runtime. Routes and nav are now generated from a\nmanifest instead of a bespoke page per remote:\n\n- src/remotes/*: manifest fetching, registerRemotes()/loadRemote() from\n  @module-federation/runtime (not the vite plugin''s `remotes` option, which\n  rewrites import() specifiers at build time and can''t support remotes\n  unknown until runtime — confirmed by reading its source), icon whitelist,\n  and manifest-entry -> Route mapping.\n- src/store/remotes: a Recoil atom that fetches the manifest once and\n  registers its remotes with the federation runtime in the same effect.\n- src/pages/DynamicModule: the one route (`/modules/:remoteId`) every\n  manifest entry resolves to, with its own Suspense/ErrorBoundary so one dead\n  remote can''t take down the shell. Reuses the theme+userProfile prop\n  contract already validated for chat_remote (Recoil/MUI singleton sharing\n  across the federation boundary doesn''t work in this stack — data crosses\n  as props, not shared Context).\n- routes/utils.ts gains use*-prefixed hooks (useDynamicRoutes,\n  useRoutesInGroup, useNavigableRoutes) that merge the static `routes` object\n  with manifest-sourced routes; Rail/BottomBar/MoreSheet/useItems now read\n  through those instead of the static-only functions.\n- chat_remote migrates to being the first manifest entry: apps/host/pages/Chat\n  and remotes.d.ts are gone, /Chat redirects to /modules/chat.\n- The manifest itself is hosted outside the host''s own deploy\n  (remotes-manifest/, a separate static Vercel project) via\n  VITE_REMOTES_MANIFEST_URL, falling back to a local copy in\n  apps/host/public/ for dev. Changing the remote list in production never\n  touches the host — not the code, not a redeploy.\n\nVerified with a real headless browser (dev and production build): nav is\nmanifest-sourced, /modules/chat renders identically to the old static page,\nthe command palette picks up manifest aliases, and a deliberately unreachable\nmanifest entry renders an isolated fallback without affecting the rest of the\nshell.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* chore: ignore .vercel/ (local project link for the manifest deploy)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix: restore .env to .gitignore\n\nThe Vercel CLI rewrote this file during an earlier `vercel deploy`/`link`\nand dropped the plain .env entry, replacing it with .env.vercel. Confirmed\napps/host/.env was never actually committed, but it needs to stay ignored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* chore(manifest): point chat_remote at ingredient-chat.vercel.app\n\nchat_remote now has its own dedicated repo (0xHackerSpace/ingredient-chat,\nbuilt from the ingredient template) instead of living inside this\nmonorepo''s apps/chat-remote. wrapper-chat-remote.vercel.app is no longer\nthe source of truth for this container.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix(deploy): add s-maxage=0 so Vercel''s CDN actually revalidates\n\nmax-age=0 alone only governs browser/shared-cache fallback behavior —\nwithout s-maxage, Vercel''s edge CDN kept serving the manifest''s previous\ncontent for hours after a new deployment went live (observed directly: the\naliased domain served stale content while the new deployment''s own\nunaliased URL already had the update). Same fix applied to the deprecated\napps/chat-remote for consistency.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix(deploy): use no-store for the remotes manifest — s-maxage=0 wasn''t enough\n\nConfirmed by direct testing: even with s-maxage=0, the aliased domain for\nthis framework:null static deployment kept serving a stale response (same\ncached headers and body) across two redeploys, while the same fix worked\nimmediately on ingredient-chat''s Vite-framework deployment. no-store is a\nstronger directive that should stop the edge from storing this response at\nall; the manifest is small and fetched rarely, so the lost caching benefit\ndoesn''t matter here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a25b601c13ccda9e879350889b76bc23093e9b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/trees/9a25b601c13ccda9e879350889b76bc23093e9b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/commits/aa47887308010f065e9f19d8656d600edad0d384","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a25b601c13ccda9e879350889b76bc23093e9b5\nparent fb1113803761500567a31036a7db773db3232e29\nauthor Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa <22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790535700 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790535700 -0300\n\nPrototype: Module Federation for the Chat microapp (#7)\n\n* chore: local changes\n\n* feat(federation): federate Chat as a Module Federation remote\n\nRestructures the repo into npm workspaces (apps/host, apps/chat-remote) to\nprototype Module Federation for shared UI components. The Chat microapp is\nextracted into its own independently buildable/deployable package and\nconsumed by the host at runtime via @module-federation/vite.\n\nCross-boundary state (MUI theme, logged-in user profile) is passed as plain\nprops into the exposed component rather than shared as a federation\nsingleton — sharing @mui/material and recoil as singletons hit real bugs in\nthis Rollup/Vite setup (circular init errors, subpath imports bypassing the\nshared scope, and Recoil never actually resolving to the host''s single\ninstance across the boundary).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix(deploy): point Vercel at apps/host/dist\n\nThe app now builds into apps/host/dist after the workspace split, so\nVercel failed with \"No Output Directory named dist found\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* chore(chat-remote): add Vercel headers for cross-origin remote loading\n\nAllows the host to fetch remoteEntry.js and its chunks from another origin\nand keeps remoteEntry.js revalidated so hosts pick up new remote builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* feat(host): make the chat remote URL configurable via CHAT_REMOTE_URL\n\nDefaults to http://localhost:5174 for local dev; set it in the build\nenvironment (Vercel) to point the host at a deployed remote.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* feat(federation): consume remotes from a runtime manifest, not vite.config.ts\n\nGeneralizes Module Federation from one hardcoded remote (chat_remote) to N\nremotes discovered at runtime. Routes and nav are now generated from a\nmanifest instead of a bespoke page per remote:\n\n- src/remotes/*: manifest fetching, registerRemotes()/loadRemote() from\n  @module-federation/runtime (not the vite plugin''s `remotes` option, which\n  rewrites import() specifiers at build time and can''t support remotes\n  unknown until runtime — confirmed by reading its source), icon whitelist,\n  and manifest-entry -> Route mapping.\n- src/store/remotes: a Recoil atom that fetches the manifest once and\n  registers its remotes with the federation runtime in the same effect.\n- src/pages/DynamicModule: the one route (`/modules/:remoteId`) every\n  manifest entry resolves to, with its own Suspense/ErrorBoundary so one dead\n  remote can''t take down the shell. Reuses the theme+userProfile prop\n  contract already validated for chat_remote (Recoil/MUI singleton sharing\n  across the federation boundary doesn''t work in this stack — data crosses\n  as props, not shared Context).\n- routes/utils.ts gains use*-prefixed hooks (useDynamicRoutes,\n  useRoutesInGroup, useNavigableRoutes) that merge the static `routes` object\n  with manifest-sourced routes; Rail/BottomBar/MoreSheet/useItems now read\n  through those instead of the static-only functions.\n- chat_remote migrates to being the first manifest entry: apps/host/pages/Chat\n  and remotes.d.ts are gone, /Chat redirects to /modules/chat.\n- The manifest itself is hosted outside the host''s own deploy\n  (remotes-manifest/, a separate static Vercel project) via\n  VITE_REMOTES_MANIFEST_URL, falling back to a local copy in\n  apps/host/public/ for dev. Changing the remote list in production never\n  touches the host — not the code, not a redeploy.\n\nVerified with a real headless browser (dev and production build): nav is\nmanifest-sourced, /modules/chat renders identically to the old static page,\nthe command palette picks up manifest aliases, and a deliberately unreachable\nmanifest entry renders an isolated fallback without affecting the rest of the\nshell.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* chore: ignore .vercel/ (local project link for the manifest deploy)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix: restore .env to .gitignore\n\nThe Vercel CLI rewrote this file during an earlier `vercel deploy`/`link`\nand dropped the plain .env entry, replacing it with .env.vercel. Confirmed\napps/host/.env was never actually committed, but it needs to stay ignored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* chore(manifest): point chat_remote at ingredient-chat.vercel.app\n\nchat_remote now has its own dedicated repo (0xHackerSpace/ingredient-chat,\nbuilt from the ingredient template) instead of living inside this\nmonorepo''s apps/chat-remote. wrapper-chat-remote.vercel.app is no longer\nthe source of truth for this container.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix(deploy): add s-maxage=0 so Vercel''s CDN actually revalidates\n\nmax-age=0 alone only governs browser/shared-cache fallback behavior —\nwithout s-maxage, Vercel''s edge CDN kept serving the manifest''s previous\ncontent for hours after a new deployment went live (observed directly: the\naliased domain served stale content while the new deployment''s own\nunaliased URL already had the update). Same fix applied to the deprecated\napps/chat-remote for consistency.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n* fix(deploy): use no-store for the remotes manifest — s-maxage=0 wasn''t enough\n\nConfirmed by direct testing: even with s-maxage=0, the aliased domain for\nthis framework:null static deployment kept serving a stale response (same\ncached headers and body) across two redeploys, while the same fix worked\nimmediately on ingredient-chat''s Vite-framework deployment. no-store is a\nstronger directive that should stop the edge from storing this response at\nall; the manifest is small and fetched rarely, so the lost caching benefit\ndoesn''t matter here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KYsKPc4CJuydwcdkCUPBdH\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquWgUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUmUQAFetsVNBJ111VT9TwyYm89vc\nIOX8TXHZ+fwP4+evuN1zFaQ+KxzWqo6j6ZuNVFIvJYFRuRKmh4cgdGkjzyVLKGlK\n+trt/U9oyBrE/eYy24UKNtJzWldknaqsiF/5Tl0oYVtCqVDp3CBSvDhSQT6XwyOf\nnFR/+S/5NpyF8dPsDEL6R+uLRY+TgdG8tTYq4EB3xDFKluJL672p2upyGp/skjpt\ncTiqHvkSfJWmOz1Pq80Pr692EFIGbg2LL8JjLTEVSH0bMVQyWsEfmhok40ssKCUM\nZ6T9WTJLlTEnD7xMJNhLyRLhAPxZynPvGW/+j5ENDYmb22xyWCw3A15Bs3lgFmtA\nHVBVl9YQqKm7z+JrnBHfksyWcmHuSrWAbKh+CLCSD2cvlcC3f2y1L4wGhVuYJemE\n6Ro1SanOmAi5ANVZLhlOmtGkXprxqrTuuCYAwAYj2laOuErBSmXllFS+O+C6Pzg8\nAVRtfdi+UpPC9rz4LrBaIki8ZxQ8gxyauSEqE/hGwOgOZCgiQc0/9/64bwY3u9+w\nPm1eGxK7iSWRQs+c3x8ZDEBQzJMSyX3SiMVj6MfHppuin7LRdubHaLhwJSWMmvZ3\nUqpRsPc5ey5UM8JFJxCQ+rZtyliJHLqdtteCUYG/ZM8PcPiGPHW248NYjJWMzV0y\nM78XHRIIXtIitP8PmmwL\n=tc7s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T19:01:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/