.com/users/IanOliv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/76600946be63934a4e1638ca40701d9a19882faa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T18:46:54Z","email":"22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T18:46:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ARfiti): rebuild the page around the map (#6)\n\nThe page was a flat green \"Base map\" rectangle with a loose \"Habilitar\ndevice\" button, a blue bar and two grey bars stacked on a light card.\nNothing on it said which element was the subject.\n\nNow the map is the page and everything else is a layer over it:\n\n- Map fills its column — dark #101520 tile ground, 74px street grid,\n  226px avenues, one soft radial glow. No card, no padding, no green.\n- Pins layer with the five states (selected, available, out of range,\n  claimed, you), a callout on the selected pin, a floating search/sort\n  bar, a status pill and the zoom/recentre stack.\n- One PieceRow component driven by `state`, rendered by both the 316px\n  desktop panel and the mobile sheet. Selection is revealed in place —\n  no route change.\n- The sheet has three detents (peek / half / full), drags from its\n  handle and holds the profile at full. The map never unmounts.\n- Scan and claim are two steps of one flow over the live map, with a\n  real getUserMedia fallback when there is no camera or it is refused.\n\nThe orphans are replaced by states: \"Habilitar device\" is gone — when\nlocation is refused the map dims and the status pill becomes the\n\"Enable location\" button; an insert shows a skeleton row plus an amber\npin, keeping a Retry if the upload fails; the profile is the sheet at\nfull rather than a route that loses the map.\n\nOne `selectedId` drives the pin, the row and the sheet, so tapping a pin\nscrolls its row into view and tapping a row pans the map to the pin.\nExactly one filled accent element is on screen at a time.\n\n`fullBleed` is a new route flag: a module can ask the shell for its\ngutter when its content is the page. The shell still owns the header,\nthe rail and the toasts.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017HRRRx282rzcaqx9Tf4cg8\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0a2ee99f4f5d2b084a0aead36ca9e4d63aab451","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/trees/f0a2ee99f4f5d2b084a0aead36ca9e4d63aab451"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/commits/76600946be63934a4e1638ca40701d9a19882faa","verification":{"payload":"tree f0a2ee99f4f5d2b084a0aead36ca9e4d63aab451\nparent b7df19c74347950fbcde37757ef10601d644ed31\nauthor Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa <22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com> 1787597214 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787597214 -0300\n\nfeat(ARfiti): rebuild the page around the map (#6)\n\nThe page was a flat green \"Base map\" rectangle with a loose \"Habilitar\ndevice\" button, a blue bar and two grey bars stacked on a light card.\nNothing on it said which element was the subject.\n\nNow the map is the page and everything else is a layer over it:\n\n- Map fills its column — dark #101520 tile ground, 74px street grid,\n  226px avenues, one soft radial glow. No card, no padding, no green.\n- Pins layer with the five states (selected, available, out of range,\n  claimed, you), a callout on the selected pin, a floating search/sort\n  bar, a status pill and the zoom/recentre stack.\n- One PieceRow component driven by `state`, rendered by both the 316px\n  desktop panel and the mobile sheet. Selection is revealed in place —\n  no route change.\n- The sheet has three detents (peek / half / full), drags from its\n  handle and holds the profile at full. The map never unmounts.\n- Scan and claim are two steps of one flow over the live map, with a\n  real getUserMedia fallback when there is no camera or it is refused.\n\nThe orphans are replaced by states: \"Habilitar device\" is gone — when\nlocation is refused the map dims and the status pill becomes the\n\"Enable location\" button; an insert shows a skeleton row plus an amber\npin, keeping a Retry if the upload fails; the profile is the sheet at\nfull rather than a route that loses the map.\n\nOne `selectedId` drives the pin, the row and the sheet, so tapping a pin\nscrolls its row into view and tapping a row pans the map to the pin.\nExactly one filled accent element is on screen at a time.\n\n`fullBleed` is a new route flag: a module can ask the shell for its\ngutter when its content is the page. The shell still owns the header,\nthe rail and the toasts.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017HRRRx282rzcaqx9Tf4cg8\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjJGeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6qEQAK1GzI6IDZP2AmAH3YzepESX\nNS3szqM3fBEeUtSWVxxmLKTDHMaxx68t2DdKfLSV6jQwPYNJ8IzRSY4d8GeoOGHz\n8hsM/VxeU3JNUJnDTmvej/Dm0OV0IMAHO9ur6ZK3usj8AXw0tr17osBuQQ3im0oV\nqQCpvsef5tmomjYLKnIvKqucPpJHqkwASpMy1dwCzrTgbl4lO3aDoR3PxK7fwGZI\n1MM/KrWQ1Uk5daq/3G6k/VctjPgCqaP4bxPsuM87nRocnsMzpl/Db5XUr4g093FQ\nJgTnB+UZtMR9xk2SckU3Bpc1beiF4f64q2HsZ3hrs3WKwr2i1aM7BItpcA3bwUdu\n3ZWjsWO4wusbcvTWZH/nqyGYs/4GUK2FlwS941SJ80xK34xp+wRG8cXAQFP5EPzS\nBXdpxIu+KcYIMeP2s5z5n3eOifZWHpHXb+T5D7I5IXxSqVS/eH9yBjYzwQE6iLqQ\nUiDLhRs1mOboX13zWDLsqAB3lVldzYoynQu/lCO40w8fFvziSQ2GT74zkQVH9oqj\n3YxG4eIdPyiOWXIaYQRbxtNStS8jAvMC6pJoh1dJtft8Sv5EewMLBtTtiF+urcaJ\n8iTKlvN4dcbwmqfWq9W/Q9YRJ9yz0dVyJKIdqnYW3EiQ+iLF+CsZtSAO51fNtaZk\nJZQeDnsQqwlHFaZLxtZQ\n=fTrs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T18:46:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/76600946be63934a4e1638ca40701d9a19882faa","node_id":"C_kwDOKB7Fj9oAKDc2NjAwOTQ2YmU2MzkzNGE0ZTE2MzhjYTQwNzAxZDlhMTk4ODJmYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/b7df19c74347950fbcde37757ef10601d644ed31","sha":"b7df19c74347950fbcde37757ef10601d644ed31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/b7df19c74347950fbcde37757ef10601d644ed31"}],"sha":"76600946be63934a4e1638ca40701d9a19882faa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/76600946be63934a4e1638ca40701d9a19882faa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22185362?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv","id":22185362,"login":"IanOliv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg1MzYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/b7df19c74347950fbcde37757ef10601d644ed31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T18:32:48Z","email":"22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T18:32:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(deck): add the /deck-development workbench route (#5)\n\n* feat(deck): add the /deck-development workbench route\n\nA redesigned deck motion playground that swaps the roles of today''s page:\nthe card gets the stage, the controls get a fixed inspector grouped by what\nthey do. `/Deck` is left exactly as it is so both can run side by side.\n\n- Stage: dot-grid ground, centred card with 26px origin leader lines so\n  positionH/positionV read as distance, a mono x/y/scale readout, a zoom\n  stepper with Center and Grid chips, Play + reset, and a scrubbable\n  timeline that replaces the loose duration slider.\n- Inspector (296px): Transform / Motion / Spawn, every slider showing its\n  live value in mono where the value is set — so the old \"left : 2.6 /\n  top : 0 / qnt : 1\" readout block is gone.\n- Under 900px the inspector becomes a 60vh bottom sheet, stage above.\n- No new global state: the same qnt/scale/duration/positionH/positionV/\n  animation/easing attributes and five spawn actions Micro/DeckArea drives\n  its cards with, held locally.\n- Nav entry lands under Labs with the experimental tag automatically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pb5fuVMuzo3BS4Fg739hKb\n\n* feat(deck): add eight more animations to the workbench\n\nThe Animation select offered Breathing and Ambient only. It now carries ten,\nincluding the Flip the mock names.\n\nNew: Flip and Sway (rotateY, with a perspective applied to the card wrapper so\nthey read as depth rather than a horizontal squeeze), Tilt, Wobble, Pop, Drift,\nFade and Glow.\n\nOptions and keyframes lived in two files, so adding one meant editing both.\nThey are now one catalogue in `animations.ts`: each entry carries its own\nkeyframes, the select is derived from it, and `keyframesFor(theme)` hands the\ncard every definition at once. Keyframes are a function of the theme, which is\nwhat lets Glow reach for the accent and restate the card''s own elevation\ninstead of stacking a second shadow on top of it.\n\nEvery animation opens and closes on the same pose, so an infinite run never\njumps and the timeline can be scrubbed to any point.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pb5fuVMuzo3BS4Fg739hKb\n\n* feat(deck): make /deck-development a keyframe motion workbench\n\nThe page could tune one card''s canned animation. It can now author a\nmulti-object one: Layers | Stage | Inspector with a timeline spanning the\nbottom, over a real animation document.\n\nThe document is the new piece of state — layers, tracks, keys, plus duration,\ntrigger, repeat, delay, stagger, speed and playhead — advanced by a single rAF\nloop that every panel reads from. Keys carry their own easing, so a curve is a\nproperty of a segment rather than of the whole animation, and position keys\ncarry spatial tangents, which is what makes the motion path an editable spline\nrather than a drawn polyline.\n\nThe deck page''s own controls map onto it rather than forking: `qnt` is how many\ncard layers exist, `scale`/`positionH`/`positionV` are the transform tracks,\n`duration` is the timeline, `animation` and `easing` write keys, and the five\nspawn actions set position. Nothing is a dropdown of canned effects any more —\nchoosing an animation lays down real keys you can then drag.\n\n- Layers: groups, multi-select, solo, hide, and preset pills that apply a whole\n  timeline to a selection.\n- Stage: three in-flow rows so it reflows, plus motion path, 3D and onion skin.\n- Inspector: rotate and opacity join the transform group, a diamond keys every\n  property at the playhead, and Custom bezier opens a handle editor whose mono\n  readout is the exact string the emitted code carries.\n- Timeline: transport, ruler, key diamonds with drag-to-retime (1/60s snap,\n  Shift frees it), marquee select, Alt-drag duplicate, Delete, double-click a\n  segment for its curve, Record, and Copy code.\n\nCopy code emits per-segment `animation-timing-function` inside each stop, which\nis how CSS lets one animation change curve partway through — so the paste is\nthe animation, not an approximation of it. Stagger lands as each card''s delay.\n\nPlayback deliberately ignores prefers-reduced-motion: it is the content of the\npage, not decoration. The shell''s own transitions are what that rule turns off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pb5fuVMuzo3BS4Fg739hKb\n\n* fix(deck): correct the workbench animations and make the page fit the viewport\n\nTwo reports: the animations behaved wrongly, and the page had to be scrolled.\n\nAnimations\n- Preset stops were written as absolute values, so picking Ambient teleported a\n  centred card to 0,0 and Breathing jumped it from scale .5 to .9. Stops are now\n  relative to the layer''s own pose — offsets for position and rotate, factors for\n  scale and opacity — and Breathing and Pop were renumbered as factors.\n- The card''s transform origin was its top-left corner, so Tilt, Sway and Flip\n  swung it around that corner instead of spinning it in place. Origin is now the\n  card''s middle, which also makes Center independent of scale.\n- Switching animation cleared every track on the selection, taking hand-placed\n  keys with it. It now clears only the outgoing animation''s own track.\n- The rAF loop read the playhead back from a ref each frame, so a batched render\n  could replay the same delta. Elapsed time is now accumulated in the loop.\n- New cards were born at 0,0 while the deck sat elsewhere; they now inherit the\n  last card''s pose. `Set left` counted from the document index (so the group\n  shifted everything by one) and overwrote x; it now fans from the first card.\n- The origin leader lines sat on a zero-height box, putting the horizontal one\n  at the card''s top edge rather than its middle.\n\nLayout\n- The workbench now fills the height the shell gives it and never exceeds it.\n  The timeline is capped at min(320px, 46%) and its rows scroll under a ruler\n  that stays put, with the playhead lifted into an overlay so it spans both and\n  never scrolls away. The stage''s 424px is now a preference rather than a floor,\n  so a short viewport shrinks it instead of growing a page scrollbar.\n- Below 900px the page still scrolls: four regions and a 60vh bottom sheet\n  cannot share a phone screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pb5fuVMuzo3BS4Fg739hKb\n\n* fix(deck): let the timeline fill its band\n\nTwo things left dead space in the timeline panel.\n\nThe track surface had a fixed `height: bodyHeight`, so it stopped at the last\nproperty row: everything below it lost its gridlines and stopped responding to\ndouble-click-to-add-key, while the gutter''s border ran on to the bottom and made\nthe gap obvious. It is now a `minHeight`, and the scroller''s single row is\n`minmax(min-content, 1fr)`, so the surface stretches to the bottom of the panel\nwhen the document is small and still scrolls when there are more tracks than fit.\n\nThe panel itself was a content-sized grid row capped by `max-height`, so it\nnever claimed the space it had. The workbench now gives the timeline a band of\nits own — `clamp(200px, 34%, 340px)` — and the panel fills it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pb5fuVMuzo3BS4Fg739hKb\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"895293807ae45be49d3af9d570aa49542c10f96c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/trees/895293807ae45be49d3af9d570aa49542c10f96c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/commits/b7df19c74347950fbcde37757ef10601d644ed31","verification":{"payload":"tree 895293807ae45be49d3af9d570aa49542c10f96c\nparent 72ce82afe3930858565a2f35f413c9deaad1cdde\nauthor Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa <22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com> 1787596368 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787596368 -0300\n\nfeat(deck): add the /deck-development workbench route (#5)\n\n* feat(deck): add the /deck-development workbench route\n\nA redesigned deck motion playground that swaps the roles of today''s page:\nthe card gets the stage, the controls get a fixed inspector grouped by what\nthey do. `/Deck` is left exactly as it is so both can run side by side.\n\n- Stage: dot-grid ground, centred card with 26px origin leader lines so\n  positionH/positionV read as distance, a mono x/y/scale readout, a zoom\n  stepper with Center and Grid chips, Play + reset, and a scrubbable\n  timeline that replaces the loose duration slider.\n- Inspector (296px): Transform / Motion / Spawn, every slider showing its\n  live value in mono where the value is set — so the old \"left : 2.6 /\n  top : 0 / qnt : 1\" readout block is gone.\n- Under 900px the inspector becomes a 60vh bottom sheet, stage above.\n- No new global state: the same qnt/scale/duration/positionH/positionV/\n  animation/easing attributes and five spawn actions Micro/DeckArea drives\n  its cards with, held locally.\n- Nav entry lands under Labs with the experimental tag automatically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pb5fuVMuzo3BS4Fg739hKb\n\n* feat(deck): add eight more animations to the workbench\n\nThe Animation select offered Breathing and Ambient only. It now carries ten,\nincluding the Flip the mock names.\n\nNew: Flip and Sway (rotateY, with a perspective applied to the card wrapper so\nthey read as depth rather than a horizontal squeeze), Tilt, Wobble, Pop, Drift,\nFade and Glow.\n\nOptions and keyframes lived in two files, so adding one meant editing both.\nThey are now one catalogue in `animations.ts`: each entry carries its own\nkeyframes, the select is derived from it, and `keyframesFor(theme)` hands the\ncard every definition at once. Keyframes are a function of the theme, which is\nwhat lets Glow reach for the accent and restate the card''s own elevation\ninstead of stacking a second shadow on top of it.\n\nEvery animation opens and closes on the same pose, so an infinite run never\njumps and the timeline can be scrubbed to any point.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pb5fuVMuzo3BS4Fg739hKb\n\n* feat(deck): make /deck-development a keyframe motion workbench\n\nThe page could tune one card''s canned animation. It can now author a\nmulti-object one: Layers | Stage | Inspector with a timeline spanning the\nbottom, over a real animation document.\n\nThe document is the new piece of state — layers, tracks, keys, plus duration,\ntrigger, repeat, delay, stagger, speed and playhead — advanced by a single rAF\nloop that every panel reads from. Keys carry their own easing, so a curve is a\nproperty of a segment rather than of the whole animation, and position keys\ncarry spatial tangents, which is what makes the motion path an editable spline\nrather than a drawn polyline.\n\nThe deck page''s own controls map onto it rather than forking: `qnt` is how many\ncard layers exist, `scale`/`positionH`/`positionV` are the transform tracks,\n`duration` is the timeline, `animation` and `easing` write keys, and the five\nspawn actions set position. Nothing is a dropdown of canned effects any more —\nchoosing an animation lays down real keys you can then drag.\n\n- Layers: groups, multi-select, solo, hide, and preset pills that apply a whole\n  timeline to a selection.\n- Stage: three in-flow rows so it reflows, plus motion path, 3D and onion skin.\n- Inspector: rotate and opacity join the transform group, a diamond keys every\n  property at the playhead, and Custom bezier opens a handle editor whose mono\n  readout is the exact string the emitted code carries.\n- Timeline: transport, ruler, key diamonds with drag-to-retime (1/60s snap,\n  Shift frees it), marquee select, Alt-drag duplicate, Delete, double-click a\n  segment for its curve, Record, and Copy code.\n\nCopy code emits per-segment `animation-timing-function` inside each stop, which\nis how CSS lets one animation change curve partway through — so the paste is\nthe animation, not an approximation of it. Stagger lands as each card''s delay.\n\nPlayback deliberately ignores prefers-reduced-motion: it is the content of the\npage, not decoration. The shell''s own transitions are what that rule turns off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pb5fuVMuzo3BS4Fg739hKb\n\n* fix(deck): correct the workbench animations and make the page fit the viewport\n\nTwo reports: the animations behaved wrongly, and the page had to be scrolled.\n\nAnimations\n- Preset stops were written as absolute values, so picking Ambient teleported a\n  centred card to 0,0 and Breathing jumped it from scale .5 to .9. Stops are now\n  relative to the layer''s own pose — offsets for position and rotate, factors for\n  scale and opacity — and Breathing and Pop were renumbered as factors.\n- The card''s transform origin was its top-left corner, so Tilt, Sway and Flip\n  swung it around that corner instead of spinning it in place. Origin is now the\n  card''s middle, which also makes Center independent of scale.\n- Switching animation cleared every track on the selection, taking hand-placed\n  keys with it. It now clears only the outgoing animation''s own track.\n- The rAF loop read the playhead back from a ref each frame, so a batched render\n  could replay the same delta. Elapsed time is now accumulated in the loop.\n- New cards were born at 0,0 while the deck sat elsewhere; they now inherit the\n  last card''s pose. `Set left` counted from the document index (so the group\n  shifted everything by one) and overwrote x; it now fans from the first card.\n- The origin leader lines sat on a zero-height box, putting the horizontal one\n  at the card''s top edge rather than its middle.\n\nLayout\n- The workbench now fills the height the shell gives it and never exceeds it.\n  The timeline is capped at min(320px, 46%) and its rows scroll under a ruler\n  that stays put, with the playhead lifted into an overlay so it spans both and\n  never scrolls away. The stage''s 424px is now a preference rather than a floor,\n  so a short viewport shrinks it instead of growing a page scrollbar.\n- Below 900px the page still scrolls: four regions and a 60vh bottom sheet\n  cannot share a phone screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pb5fuVMuzo3BS4Fg739hKb\n\n* fix(deck): let the timeline fill its band\n\nTwo things left dead space in the timeline panel.\n\nThe track surface had a fixed `height: bodyHeight`, so it stopped at the last\nproperty row: everything below it lost its gridlines and stopped responding to\ndouble-click-to-add-key, while the gutter''s border ran on to the bottom and made\nthe gap obvious. It is now a `minHeight`, and the scroller''s single row is\n`minmax(min-content, 1fr)`, so the surface stretches to the bottom of the panel\nwhen the document is small and still scrolls when there are more tracks than fit.\n\nThe panel itself was a content-sized grid row capped by `max-height`, so it\nnever claimed the space it had. The workbench now gives the timeline a band of\nits own — `clamp(200px, 34%, 340px)` — and the panel fills it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pb5fuVMuzo3BS4Fg739hKb\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjI5QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI+IQAG7YiHjJdvGJWomRTRHhM/V2\nS7acILMPm7QZQm4SENfD4ylmVYpZPdGu6ppQ/qQEzw9wh9WAnojh+2K2JFk8Pd5K\nBlaVzxnk/EE4Br2HAI9L3VPzADXUcGLV08gVtIN7LnaEwkenTzvKaGSi767m/mbw\np5/vEup5g2cnRavXOtaLAnDLBfpg1ur6McieZ3MHWYrzldpUNHIMBbY3j3jve35l\nSUyftNH/n1YdE6UNzoEAIs5mx9iNk1e/a5bA4/wQzDm0ycxBbrZoEC8aVrMCuiyX\nADZwBzZVQm5d/31lQvlIpgxfff1PhgVuSKkJRadAUr1OFPm9ab9GOQI1ik5J8FUB\nPs1vnCjqaTyRSBDBOQUG+c2KQIW8wBQqFTXg5/wtfyLyK596O4/eme64doPY2Bhi\nZFkHC+jyMZGXOTZOq8tWlIDvXPIn7TyJGvmbhhbPHPtNphXli5VrmIPfGDHsxNbW\nEtn9WY39nxPqblfbErdvn+e1Fg50/mbLyR7SIipOXgX6hl73/dUiK62LPei/z9p2\nwZR/Q8tnSAu6ReBq+tSN5al5JHVRWp+cOCNXwiEOwoGbupTQC/dBg1TAjhx2oJIM\nWXnJPcIZH9YJRaerhy2PtjgfA4w9fKoHq71Jd3/kT3jlzGWjkq3aSouUFLBEhxDH\nAdnFI359kBEltBWsnLgL\n=wfUG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T18:32:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/b7df19c74347950fbcde37757ef10601d644ed31","node_id":"C_kwDOKB7Fj9oAKGI3ZGYxOWM3NDM0Nzk1MGZiY2RlMzc3NTdlZjEwNjAxZDY0NGVkMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv/wrapper/commit/72ce82afe3930858565a2f35f413c9deaad1cdde","sha":"72ce82afe3930858565a2f35f413c9deaad1cdde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/72ce82afe3930858565a2f35f413c9deaad1cdde"}],"sha":"b7df19c74347950fbcde37757ef10601d644ed31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/b7df19c74347950fbcde37757ef10601d644ed31"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22185362?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/IanOliv","id":22185362,"login":"IanOliv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTg1MzYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanOliv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/commits/72ce82afe3930858565a2f35f413c9deaad1cdde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T16:28:07Z","email":"22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T16:28:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(shell): apply the Wrapper design system (#4)\n\n* chore: local changes\n\n* feat(shell): apply the Wrapper design system\n\nImplements the \"Instrument\" direction from the design handoff: one dark\nground, one accent, identity from typography and density rather than paint.\n\nTheme\n- Full dark + light palettes (drawn, not inverted), type scale, base-8\n  spacing, four elevation levels with MUI''s other 20 aliased down, motion\n  tokens, and a `theme.shell` namespace for what MUI''s palette has no home\n  for. One `prefers-reduced-motion` hook in the theme, not per component.\n- Inter Variable and JetBrains Mono, self-hosted, latin subset only,\n  replacing the four Helvetica @font-face rules (which pointed at files the\n  repo never had, in a stylesheet nothing imported).\n- New `/__tokens` dev route rendering every token and component state.\n\nNavigation\n- The drawer goes: a 72px pinnable rail on desktop, a bottom bar plus a\n  \"More\" sheet on mobile. Active state is carried three ways at once —\n  fill-weight icon, a sliding 2px accent rule, and a tinted ground.\n- Routes regrouped into Modules / Labs / Account / hidden, with Phosphor\n  icons chosen semantically. `/` now redirects to `/card`; the duplicate\n  Welcome entry is gone.\n\nShell surfaces\n- Header carries the mark, the module name, \"Jump to…\" and the avatar; the\n  GitHub link moved into the account menu.\n- New ⌘K command palette: grouped results, alias matching, key caps,\n  recents, and a mobile sheet variant. The hotkeys dialog folds into it.\n- Toasts, loading skeletons and both error screens rebuilt on the tokens.\n  Semantic color is a text color and a 2px mark, never a filled bar.\n\nScreens\n- Card feed, sensor panel and sign-in built to the mockups; chat and\n  register rebuilt from the tokens since they were never designed.\n\nAlso fixes a crash on first load (notistack v3 rejects an undefined\nmessage), drops a ~400KB lorem-ipsum corpus from the bundle, and sets\nmanifest/meta theme colors so the phone no longer flashes white on launch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(card): centre the detail panel and make it behave like a modal\n\nThe panel was centred with `transform: translateX(-50%)` and anchored 8vh\nfrom the top. Two problems with that.\n\nVertically it was never centred at all: 72px above and 244px below on a\n900px viewport, and 96/520 on a 1200px one — the taller the screen, the\nmore it hung. On mobile it stuck to the top and left 159px of dead\nbackdrop at the base.\n\nHorizontally it was centred only sometimes. framer-motion owns `transform`\non a `layoutId` element, and in production the `translateX(-50%)` was being\ndropped, leaving the panel hanging off `left: 50%`. Centring now comes from\nthe Modal''s flexbox: free space cannot be overwritten by an animation, a\ntransform can. The panel''s computed transform is `none` in every case.\n\nWrapping it in MUI''s Modal also brings the escape key, a focus trap and\n`aria-modal` — none of which it had. The scroll lock is ours, because MUI\nonly knows how to freeze `document.body` and this shell scrolls an inner\n`<main>`; `useScrollLock` walks up from the module''s own root rather than\nquerying for shell chrome, so the module still doesn''t need to know what\nthe shell''s layout looks like. The close button moved outside the scrolling\narea so it stays reachable on long content.\n\n`/card/:id` now has a title, so the header reads \"Cards\" instead of falling\nback to the app name. That would have put a duplicate \"Cards\" row in ⌘K\npointing at the literal `/card/:id`, so `isNavigable` now excludes routes\nwith a path parameter.\n\nVerified at 1280x900, 1280x1200, 1728x1000 and 390x844: centred on both\naxes, mobile filling to the base, real wheel events blocked behind the\npanel, focus trapped, escape closing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9022bf255390f2b23c12286b7b179047e8a1e9be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/trees/9022bf255390f2b23c12286b7b179047e8a1e9be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IanOliv/wrapper/git/commits/72ce82afe3930858565a2f35f413c9deaad1cdde","verification":{"payload":"tree 9022bf255390f2b23c12286b7b179047e8a1e9be\nparent 25cd8edd5e125740c6662d03ac5f7428e250acb5\nauthor Ian Gabriel Oliveira de Sousa <22185362+IanOliv@users.noreply.github.com> 1785860887 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785860887 -0300\n\nfeat(shell): apply the Wrapper design system (#4)\n\n* chore: local changes\n\n* feat(shell): apply the Wrapper design system\n\nImplements the \"Instrument\" direction from the design handoff: one dark\nground, one accent, identity from typography and density rather than paint.\n\nTheme\n- Full dark + light palettes (drawn, not inverted), type scale, base-8\n  spacing, four elevation levels with MUI''s other 20 aliased down, motion\n  tokens, and a `theme.shell` namespace for what MUI''s palette has no home\n  for. One `prefers-reduced-motion` hook in the theme, not per component.\n- Inter Variable and JetBrains Mono, self-hosted, latin subset only,\n  replacing the four Helvetica @font-face rules (which pointed at files the\n  repo never had, in a stylesheet nothing imported).\n- New `/__tokens` dev route rendering every token and component state.\n\nNavigation\n- The drawer goes: a 72px pinnable rail on desktop, a bottom bar plus a\n  \"More\" sheet on mobile. Active state is carried three ways at once —\n  fill-weight icon, a sliding 2px accent rule, and a tinted ground.\n- Routes regrouped into Modules / Labs / Account / hidden, with Phosphor\n  icons chosen semantically. `/` now redirects to `/card`; the duplicate\n  Welcome entry is gone.\n\nShell surfaces\n- Header carries the mark, the module name, \"Jump to…\" and the avatar; the\n  GitHub link moved into the account menu.\n- New ⌘K command palette: grouped results, alias matching, key caps,\n  recents, and a mobile sheet variant. The hotkeys dialog folds into it.\n- Toasts, loading skeletons and both error screens rebuilt on the tokens.\n  Semantic color is a text color and a 2px mark, never a filled bar.\n\nScreens\n- Card feed, sensor panel and sign-in built to the mockups; chat and\n  register rebuilt from the tokens since they were never designed.\n\nAlso fixes a crash on first load (notistack v3 rejects an undefined\nmessage), drops a ~400KB lorem-ipsum corpus from the bundle, and sets\nmanifest/meta theme colors so the phone no longer flashes white on launch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(card): centre the detail panel and make it behave like a modal\n\nThe panel was centred with `transform: translateX(-50%)` and anchored 8vh\nfrom the top. Two problems with that.\n\nVertically it was never centred at all: 72px above and 244px below on a\n900px viewport, and 96/520 on a 1200px one — the taller the screen, the\nmore it hung. On mobile it stuck to the top and left 159px of dead\nbackdrop at the base.\n\nHorizontally it was centred only sometimes. framer-motion owns `transform`\non a `layoutId` element, and in production the `translateX(-50%)` was being\ndropped, leaving the panel hanging off `left: 50%`. Centring now comes from\nthe Modal''s flexbox: free space cannot be overwritten by an animation, a\ntransform can. The panel''s computed transform is `none` in every case.\n\nWrapping it in MUI''s Modal also brings the escape key, a focus trap and\n`aria-modal` — none of which it had. The scroll lock is ours, because MUI\nonly knows how to freeze `document.body` and this shell scrolls an inner\n`<main>`; `useScrollLock` walks up from the module''s own root rather than\nquerying for shell chrome, so the module still doesn''t need to know what\nthe shell''s layout looks like. The close button moved outside the scrolling\narea so it stays reachable on long content.\n\n`/card/:id` now has a title, so the header reads \"Cards\" instead of falling\nback to the app name. That would have put a duplicate \"Cards\" row in ⌘K\npointing at the literal `/card/:id`, so `isNavigable` now excludes routes\nwith a path parameter.\n\nVerified at 1280x900, 1280x1200, 1728x1000 and 390x844: centred on both\naxes, mobile filling to the base, real wheel events blocked behind the\npanel, focus trapped, escape closing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqchMXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2hgQABChLkNPlQtSR6Pbon9Mr/Up\nRZ1l8v4qFAgQc1ixsUXcMl9T5nG6aaC7cjZPv88suCLBy6p8vQ+k9rek0gu75Do/\n6vlJN2HR3sacTyZfZnGKrVhkLoTlCocwfAR1IO9piwiMxhAIZLSj2Oqg7jKk1Oy9\neiz10pUthTszAOD9KxZaoD/2S4onqUpnzbvKqkDxFrc2IDaQGGAAuKt06ka/X6TU\nVs47uZGEvKTqEyQjrf3aO0s2JlqOF4Vf88UpjbEX8gfZ5biL1RLyKrG7LFk11u6g\nqa91NCXHX7uyIvvmf1i7yu2CekDn+C1NdDSA2hn5hJegtU6Ip4qjmCkb1i3XkzwA\nUEEPWNbVJvgPW4J3iZYpMFxLaFkTuZlcYw1vW6aMhRQpRm0HA36PvW8o0TNQ2u/X\nfdQGcfS85ZklLh+sfevso7+MRxpY75PV2JDxzqq0ZuDay4ahhwnpM+Bnn4xF3PW4\nG4r7f/ul2XNYJPWb68mTsWc/KUS+y10veJNgOh1le8sBLHLp1ddQA7gfD5NtU1MW\nCjfg1n3StyYqAGwuSHMkMbnJB0ASBEs43LbHW9ens/VAUGKm6adTuXYpqLmJRExA\nDydeqZ3E1Y2GS00k/7fhnwnjFL80ZfHuaGRvfozL1xxz8fTwBUfvDnToKRrGHL0r\nRwqsx5wz6xHs4AW5PqDU\n=sdvb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-04T16:28:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url